WEBVTT

00:15.765 --> 00:17.809
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

00:17.892 --> 00:19.477
Please stay with me, ma'am.

00:19.978 --> 00:21.062
Oh, Doctor,

00:21.896 --> 00:23.565
-I feel so tired.
-Stay awake,

00:23.648 --> 00:24.649
Open your eyes!

00:24.733 --> 00:26.317
You need to stay awake, okay?

00:26.401 --> 00:28.695
-It's so cold in here.
-Keep your eyes open!

00:29.487 --> 00:30.113
Listen ma'am,

00:30.697 --> 00:32.323
can you tell me what your name is?

00:32.407 --> 00:33.408
Seo,

00:34.909 --> 00:35.577
Eun-ju.

00:36.077 --> 00:37.537
Great, and where are you?

00:38.163 --> 00:40.165
What day is it?
Hey, ma'am, can you tell me today's date?

00:40.248 --> 00:42.000
Please tell me what the date is!

00:43.084 --> 00:45.336
You just had your second child today,
what day is it?

00:45.837 --> 00:47.005
The sixteenth,

00:47.881 --> 00:48.965
October sixteenth…

00:49.549 --> 00:50.216
Her birthday, yes.

00:50.800 --> 00:51.718
Just hang in there.

01:00.060 --> 01:02.395
We need more blood,
please. And add some more FFP too.

01:07.233 --> 01:08.109
We need CPR.

01:08.193 --> 01:09.194
We've gotta start compressions.

01:09.277 --> 01:10.320
You handle the packing and close her up.

01:10.403 --> 01:11.613
Please bring me the crash cart.

01:11.696 --> 01:13.114
-Yes.
-I need gauze.

01:24.375 --> 01:25.460
Surgical drape.

01:29.798 --> 01:30.673
I can take over.

01:34.385 --> 01:35.553
Check her epinephrine level.

01:47.816 --> 01:48.691
You still need,

01:49.192 --> 01:50.527
to feed and hold

01:50.610 --> 01:52.821
your little babies, they need you.

01:54.572 --> 01:56.991
You wanted to meet your baby so much.

02:00.620 --> 02:01.496
Eun-ju!

02:02.664 --> 02:03.498
Honey!

02:06.626 --> 02:07.502
Eun-ju!

02:09.879 --> 02:13.007
Your babies need you!
We all still need you, Eun-Ju, please,

02:13.091 --> 02:15.009
don't leave us like this, you can't!

02:18.221 --> 02:21.349
Eun-Ju!
How am I supposed to live without you?

02:55.592 --> 02:57.677
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

03:07.145 --> 03:07.812
Ah.

03:08.313 --> 03:10.064
Doctor Da-hye's on break for now, right?

03:10.148 --> 03:10.857
Yeah.

03:11.357 --> 03:14.402
She was pretty devastated by the transfer
patient's death, apparently.

03:14.485 --> 03:16.613
She kept crying about
it non-stop for days.

03:17.238 --> 03:18.239
I completely get it.

03:19.157 --> 03:21.492
We saw her getting wheeled past
us as they brought her down.

03:21.576 --> 03:23.494
Just a glimpse,
but I've still had nightmares.

03:23.995 --> 03:25.038
Yeah,

03:25.121 --> 03:27.123
she bled so much that they gave her almost
thirty whole units of blood after

03:27.207 --> 03:28.666
they had to take out her uterus.

03:28.750 --> 03:30.543
And when she got DIC,
then there was nothing much

03:30.627 --> 03:31.669
to be done at that point.

03:31.753 --> 03:32.670
It's awful.

03:33.421 --> 03:35.590
Postpartum hemorrhage is the
worst thing in the world.

03:35.673 --> 03:37.217
What causes it to start, anyway?

03:37.300 --> 03:38.051
Good question.

03:38.551 --> 03:39.677
What does cause it to start?

03:39.761 --> 03:40.929
-Hello.
-Hello, Professor.

03:41.429 --> 03:42.722
Truth is, no one knows.

03:43.681 --> 03:44.557
Not only that,

03:44.641 --> 03:46.517
but anticipating which
patient will develop

03:46.601 --> 03:48.228
PPH is currently impossible, right?

03:49.437 --> 03:51.689
We can't predict or prevent
bleeding from happening.

03:51.773 --> 03:53.983
But we can make sure we're
ready to handle it.

03:54.067 --> 03:56.236
And to be ready,
we must study the subject thoroughly.

03:56.319 --> 03:57.153
Mm.

03:57.820 --> 03:59.489
To accomplish that,
we'll increase our study

03:59.572 --> 04:00.782
sessions to twice a week.

04:00.865 --> 04:01.950
-Ugh.
-Ugh, Professor.

04:02.033 --> 04:04.869
You all seem so excited,
how about three times a week?

04:06.371 --> 04:08.289
This week,
we'll learn how a PPH situation

04:08.373 --> 04:09.457
can be ideally handled,

04:09.540 --> 04:11.501
and what sort of actions we can take,

04:11.584 --> 04:12.502
to best address it.

04:13.878 --> 04:14.629
Show me this.

04:15.129 --> 04:18.675
Professor Kong gave us this packet about
PPH in one of the previous sessions.

04:20.885 --> 04:21.719
Mm…

04:23.680 --> 04:24.430
Forget about this.

04:27.767 --> 04:28.643
Just use mine.

04:28.726 --> 04:29.560
Kay.

04:32.230 --> 04:33.898
Starting today, in these sessions,

04:33.982 --> 04:35.733
we'll learn some very important things.

04:35.817 --> 04:36.609
Not just theoretical,

04:37.110 --> 04:38.319
but practical knowledge.

04:38.903 --> 04:42.031
So I will also not tolerate anyone
nodding off or getting drowsy,

04:43.741 --> 04:45.535
or any types of similar distractions.

04:46.828 --> 04:47.704
Got it.

04:51.499 --> 04:52.500
Let's get started.

04:53.251 --> 04:55.420
The most important thing
in a PPH situation is

04:56.129 --> 04:59.048
to notice the bleeding as soon
as possible and move quickly.

05:00.758 --> 05:01.592
PPH?

05:02.302 --> 05:04.012
But I already covered that with you all.

05:04.095 --> 05:04.762
Yes.

05:05.263 --> 05:06.848
Hang on, so why is Professor Seo Jung-man-

05:06.931 --> 05:07.807
uh, sorry,

05:07.890 --> 05:09.058
Seo Jung-min re-teaching it?

05:09.142 --> 05:09.767
Ah,

05:10.268 --> 05:11.686
with what happened recently,
she's focusing,

05:11.769 --> 05:14.439
on practical knowledge to make
it simpler for us all to manage.

05:14.522 --> 05:15.440
Simpler?

05:16.024 --> 05:16.566
Hold up.

05:17.066 --> 05:18.276
You're saying I made
it hard to understand?

05:18.359 --> 05:19.193
No.

05:19.944 --> 05:22.322
She thinks she can teach about
PPH better than I can?

05:23.031 --> 05:24.615
She has to be better at everything.

05:24.699 --> 05:25.783
She's such a…

05:25.867 --> 05:27.035
raging narcissist, seriously

05:29.329 --> 05:30.830
Our surgery today is at three?

05:31.372 --> 05:32.498
Oh, actually,

05:33.082 --> 05:35.043
it looks like Professor Seo
planned for six surgeries,

05:35.126 --> 05:37.462
then there was an emergency
C-section she had to do,

05:37.545 --> 05:39.213
and a spinal block failed,
so that surgery,

05:39.297 --> 05:40.506
got pushed over to GA, and so,

05:40.590 --> 05:43.343
it ended up taking a lot longer
than anyone expected it would.

05:43.426 --> 05:44.302
So what?

05:44.385 --> 05:46.179
-When is ours?
-Around five PM

05:46.262 --> 05:48.014
The patient's been told, I just made sure.

05:48.097 --> 05:48.681
What?

05:49.182 --> 05:50.141
Hey,

05:50.224 --> 05:51.768
this is the only surgery I have scheduled.

05:51.851 --> 05:54.062
You really expect me to wait
until five pm tonight?

05:54.145 --> 05:54.979
Uh-

05:55.605 --> 05:58.900
Well, Professor Seo has been given
priority use of the OR today…

05:59.609 --> 06:01.819
She's controlling the entire OR schedule,
huh?

06:01.903 --> 06:03.196
She wants to push me around…

06:04.697 --> 06:05.656
In that case

06:05.740 --> 06:07.575
Make Anesthesia open another OR for us.

06:07.658 --> 06:08.284
Oh,

06:08.785 --> 06:09.952
they said they could do
two surgeries at once,

06:10.036 --> 06:12.872
after they wrap up the GS surgery
planned for three o'clock,

06:12.955 --> 06:14.999
but Professor Seo has booked
that room, too, apparently.

06:15.083 --> 06:19.003
If they're opening two, I'm entitled to
one. Why does she get to take everything?

06:19.087 --> 06:19.837
Wait a minute.

06:20.338 --> 06:21.923
Is this an attempt to assert dominance?

06:22.006 --> 06:22.757
It's not!

06:23.257 --> 06:25.218
I would guess she's probably
way too overloaded to,

06:25.301 --> 06:26.969
pull anything like that right now.

06:29.180 --> 06:32.683
Yi-young said that she has to attend a
meeting with the hospital director at

06:32.767 --> 06:33.768
about six thirty or so,

06:34.268 --> 06:37.146
and needs to finish her all work before
she goes, so she's asking you to

06:37.230 --> 06:38.106
understand the issue.

06:38.189 --> 06:39.649
Why is she meeting the hospital director?

06:39.732 --> 06:41.567
I wouldn't really know about that,
I'm sorry.

06:41.651 --> 06:42.652
That little-

06:43.403 --> 06:45.113
Tell Seo Jung-min that I
go into surgery at three,

06:45.196 --> 06:47.448
and that there's no way I'm going
to wait until five o'clock.

06:47.532 --> 06:49.200
Make sure you book that
room for me or else.

06:49.283 --> 06:50.993
-You got that?
-Oh,

06:51.077 --> 06:51.911
uh-

06:54.872 --> 06:57.291
Ugh, how am I supposed to do all of that,
huh?

06:58.501 --> 07:00.878
You told Professor Kong her surgery's
been pushed back, right?

07:00.962 --> 07:01.879
Yes, I informed her.

07:01.963 --> 07:04.757
She knows she has the final slot today,
as we discussed.

07:05.466 --> 07:06.467
And she agreed to it?

07:06.551 --> 07:07.927
She didn't fight you?

07:08.010 --> 07:09.387
I don't know.
All I really care about right

07:09.470 --> 07:10.430
now is my own survival.

07:14.600 --> 07:15.351
Oh, I mean,

07:15.935 --> 07:16.978
you told me I had to,

07:17.061 --> 07:19.605
make sure you'd be done with
your surgeries by six.

07:20.857 --> 07:21.524
If I didn't,

07:22.024 --> 07:22.775
I know you'd,

07:23.276 --> 07:24.527
scold me about it…

07:28.364 --> 07:28.990
Well, good job.

07:30.116 --> 07:31.200
That's a change.

07:31.284 --> 07:32.410
What's going on here?

07:46.174 --> 07:49.177
Okay, I'm grabbing Tuesday for Professor
Kong's induction case, seem fair?

07:49.260 --> 07:50.136
No, you can't.

07:50.636 --> 07:53.890
Professor Seo asked me to get a
room for an induction that day.

07:53.973 --> 07:54.807
Look,

07:55.475 --> 07:58.186
Professor Seo booked three more
on Monday already, though, right?

07:58.269 --> 07:59.103
Yeah.

07:59.645 --> 08:01.147
So we need two on Tuesday, then.

08:01.230 --> 08:03.024
You don't have many patients,
we have a ton.

08:03.524 --> 08:04.692
Why not do Thursday?

08:04.775 --> 08:06.569
Mm-mm, she'll be at a conference that day.

08:06.652 --> 08:08.821
-You can book Thursday.
-Professor Seo--

08:10.698 --> 08:11.991
JM's going to the conference too.

08:12.074 --> 08:13.451
She'll be pissed if I don't get Tuesday.

08:13.534 --> 08:14.535
What about Ggong? Knowing her,

08:14.619 --> 08:15.453
you think she'll be alright

08:15.536 --> 08:16.537
with that either?

08:16.621 --> 08:17.830
Ugh, this is really annoying.

08:18.331 --> 08:20.291
Why don't they manage
it between themselves?

08:20.374 --> 08:21.375
Exactly.

08:23.085 --> 08:23.794
Hey,

08:24.295 --> 08:26.255
don't you think the two professors
are a bit weird lately?

08:26.339 --> 08:28.508
They always were,
so I'm not surprised they still are.

08:28.591 --> 08:29.842
Yeah, I know that, still,

08:30.551 --> 08:32.261
it seems they may have gotten worse.

08:32.345 --> 08:34.764
-How so?
-I mean their rivalry, you know?

08:36.098 --> 08:36.891
They're so childish.

08:42.772 --> 08:43.523
I mean,

08:44.023 --> 08:46.108
one bristles when someone mentions
Seo Jung-min at all.

08:46.192 --> 08:49.445
The other blocks Kong Gi-sun from ever
getting anything she wants. Hm?

08:52.698 --> 08:53.741
And look,

08:53.824 --> 08:55.826
we end up dealing with all this,
stuck right in the middle

08:55.910 --> 08:56.827
of their crazy fight.

08:59.872 --> 09:00.873
Hello! Hello!

09:00.957 --> 09:01.999
What is it?

09:02.083 --> 09:03.417
Why are you here again?

09:04.085 --> 09:05.753
Im Dong-ju's got an emergency C-section.

09:05.836 --> 09:07.004
Yeah, but you're in Gynecology.

09:07.088 --> 09:07.713
Yes,

09:08.214 --> 09:09.173
I finished that work.

09:09.257 --> 09:10.341
Then why aren't you getting out of here?

09:10.424 --> 09:11.676
Why be there when you don't have to be?

09:11.759 --> 09:13.719
How can I go home when it's
an incarceration case?

09:13.803 --> 09:15.513
What do you mean?
Simple, just split and run.

09:15.596 --> 09:17.431
It's a really rare case,
so this one could be my

09:17.515 --> 09:18.599
only chance to see it.

09:21.519 --> 09:22.520
You're not going to sit in?

09:23.271 --> 09:24.146
I'm going.

09:24.230 --> 09:25.314
Home, right?

09:25.398 --> 09:26.691
Alright. See you later.

09:33.906 --> 09:34.490
Hello.

09:34.991 --> 09:35.908
Hey.

09:35.992 --> 09:37.994
You're done in the ward,
why aren't you heading out?

09:38.077 --> 09:39.954
There's a surgery I want to sit in on.

09:42.623 --> 09:43.499
You want to

09:43.583 --> 09:45.501
see this surgery so much that you're
willing to stay here late instead of

09:45.585 --> 09:46.961
going home?

09:47.587 --> 09:48.421
Yes.

09:49.422 --> 09:50.172
That's fair.

09:50.673 --> 09:52.883
This isn't an easy surgery,
and it does involve a unique approach.

09:52.967 --> 09:55.428
From a resident's point of view,
it'll be fascinating,

09:55.511 --> 09:57.805
to see the manual technique
that's involved, I'm sure.

09:57.888 --> 09:59.724
-Yeah.
-I think it's truly impressive.

10:03.019 --> 10:04.353
-Aw-
-Well, then.

10:04.979 --> 10:05.980
Where are you going?

10:06.647 --> 10:08.065
The room changed, it's here.

10:08.149 --> 10:09.066
No, it's not.

10:09.567 --> 10:11.902
Professor Im's doing the
C-section in OR six.

10:13.904 --> 10:14.572
Hey,

10:15.072 --> 10:16.782
you're on the Gynecology rotation, though.

10:16.866 --> 10:19.744
Yes, but I heard incarceration cases are
unique right from the first incision,

10:19.827 --> 10:21.037
so I really want to see this.

10:22.997 --> 10:24.081
I'll see you tomorrow.

10:28.252 --> 10:29.086
Huh.

10:29.712 --> 10:30.630
What the-

10:32.465 --> 10:34.258
Wow, what am I going to do with her?

10:39.180 --> 10:40.014
Hey!

10:41.474 --> 10:43.976
Why did you call me when you
haven't finished prepping?

10:44.477 --> 10:45.311
Ah.

10:46.395 --> 10:48.189
Should I have stayed back
to watch the surgery?

10:48.272 --> 10:49.607
Don't you have dinner plans?

10:49.690 --> 10:52.902
Dinner plans can get rescheduled.
Sa-bi said that this case is pretty rare.

10:52.985 --> 10:55.196
Incar… su… rround?

10:56.322 --> 10:57.740
-Incarceration.
-Yeah,

10:57.823 --> 10:58.949
that's the one.

10:59.450 --> 11:00.493
Is this really about the surgery?

11:00.576 --> 11:01.285
Good question.

11:01.786 --> 11:03.204
Is it the surgery you'd like to see?

11:03.287 --> 11:05.206
Or is it the Hello Girl
you'd possibly run into?

11:05.289 --> 11:07.291
Why would I wanna see her?
What d'you mean, huh?

11:07.375 --> 11:09.502
What do you think?
You follow the poor woman almost

11:09.585 --> 11:10.920
every chance you get lately.

11:11.003 --> 11:12.296
So I was just wondering.

11:12.380 --> 11:13.089
Follow her? When?

11:13.589 --> 11:14.882
Ever since the karaoke room dance.

11:14.965 --> 11:15.800
Hmm.

11:16.509 --> 11:17.426
That's just 'cause,

11:17.927 --> 11:19.303
we're nearly done as R Ones,

11:19.387 --> 11:20.471
then we're all R Twos.

11:21.555 --> 11:23.766
Sa-bi explains things well,
so I end up learning a lot.

11:23.849 --> 11:26.394
She can take a complicated idea and
talk it through so I understand.

11:26.477 --> 11:27.728
-Mm-hm.
-Alright, sure.

11:28.688 --> 11:30.606
Well, if you get together,
you better tell us first,

11:30.690 --> 11:31.357
before anyone else.

11:31.857 --> 11:32.775
After all,

11:33.275 --> 11:35.861
we're together sixteen plus hours a day.
If we hear it from rumors, I'll be pissed

11:35.945 --> 11:37.071
-off.
-What, are you writing a

11:37.154 --> 11:38.948
screenplay? You're being ridiculous.

11:43.703 --> 11:44.537
Hello?

11:46.122 --> 11:46.997
At the hospital.

11:49.041 --> 11:49.542
Oh!

11:50.042 --> 11:50.668
Yeah, that sounds-

11:51.961 --> 11:53.045
uh, fine.

11:53.963 --> 11:54.714
Yes.

11:58.384 --> 11:58.926
Hm?

11:59.427 --> 12:00.302
Who was that?

12:00.886 --> 12:01.429
Do you have a…?

12:02.012 --> 12:02.596
My brother-in-law.

12:03.097 --> 12:03.806
Nobody else.

12:04.390 --> 12:06.517
I'm getting a ride,
so he just called to say here's here,

12:06.600 --> 12:07.852
-that's all.
-Oh!

12:08.352 --> 12:10.229
Hey, drop me at the bus station,
then, please, okay?

12:10.312 --> 12:12.648
-It's real close by, and it's on your way.
-Hey, I can go, too!

12:12.732 --> 12:14.775
We could meet your sister's
husband, how's that sound?

12:14.859 --> 12:15.568
No you can't!

12:16.152 --> 12:16.902
-Whoa, hey!
-What?

12:16.986 --> 12:17.862
Why not?

12:17.945 --> 12:18.988
You just can't.

12:19.488 --> 12:20.614
Family discussion.

12:21.532 --> 12:22.575
It's really private.

12:22.658 --> 12:24.034
I'll just cover both my ears, then.

12:24.118 --> 12:25.536
-Eh.
-Yeah! I can, too!

12:25.619 --> 12:26.495
No, you can't.

12:26.579 --> 12:27.413
Please?

12:27.496 --> 12:29.582
I don't have the energy
to make myself walk.

12:29.665 --> 12:30.583
Can't you?

12:31.083 --> 12:31.709
Sorry, no can do.

12:31.792 --> 12:33.544
-Come on, you totally could!
-Uh-

12:34.128 --> 12:35.129
With him, it's just-

12:36.547 --> 12:37.506
He's really shy.

12:38.424 --> 12:40.885
Carpooling with someone he
doesn't know is really hard.

12:42.136 --> 12:44.555
Next time,
okay? I'll give you a ride another day.

12:44.638 --> 12:45.598
Go.

12:47.266 --> 12:48.392
Oh Yi-young…

12:50.728 --> 12:51.645
you're a real jerk.

12:52.855 --> 12:53.939
Later, then.

12:54.815 --> 12:55.733
Yeah, bye.

12:56.817 --> 12:57.818
Such a jerk!

13:19.924 --> 13:20.508
What,

13:21.008 --> 13:22.176
should I go to you?

13:22.843 --> 13:23.761
What, what-

13:24.386 --> 13:25.012
Eating?

13:25.513 --> 13:26.555
Go?

13:27.681 --> 13:28.933
Oh, I missed you a bunch, too!

13:32.353 --> 13:33.521
Just wait in the car for you?

13:34.146 --> 13:35.272
You getting in, too?

13:36.023 --> 13:37.441
W- w- what should I not do?

13:37.942 --> 13:39.819
You want me to wait in the car, right?

13:41.111 --> 13:41.695
Well, come on!

13:51.205 --> 13:52.623
What happens if we get seen?

13:55.918 --> 13:56.836
You told me before,

13:57.586 --> 13:59.713
that folks would assume
we were carpooling.

14:00.798 --> 14:01.340
Back then,

14:01.924 --> 14:03.634
that was actually the truth, so it worked.

14:03.717 --> 14:05.177
Now it's completely different.

14:06.512 --> 14:07.596
You lost me, I'm sorry.

14:07.680 --> 14:10.474
We're still carpooling the
way we always have been.

14:11.016 --> 14:11.976
It's just…

14:13.686 --> 14:14.728
If anyone at work…

14:14.812 --> 14:16.230
learns about us…

14:16.730 --> 14:18.274
I just don't want anyone to know.

14:18.357 --> 14:19.525
Why is that?

14:21.110 --> 14:22.862
In case you tell someone we're dating,

14:22.945 --> 14:24.780
and we break up soon afterward,
is that it?

14:25.739 --> 14:26.657
How can you say that?

14:26.740 --> 14:27.867
We're never breaking up.

14:30.828 --> 14:31.704
Hey listen…

14:32.538 --> 14:34.373
I've been keeping the R Ones in the dark.

14:35.499 --> 14:37.960
I should be the one to tell them first,
y'know

14:38.460 --> 14:40.462
But where do I even start
to explain all this?

14:40.546 --> 14:42.840
We first started as only in-laws,
nothing else…

14:42.923 --> 14:44.425
we were living under the same roof…

14:44.508 --> 14:47.803
We didn't plan on things to go this way,
but now that it happened-

14:48.679 --> 14:51.432
Ugh, this is giving me a really
bad headache, I can't.

14:51.515 --> 14:53.058
They're your friends,
you better tell them or else

14:53.142 --> 14:54.727
it'll hurt their feelings,
don't you think?

14:54.810 --> 14:55.978
No, they're not friends.

14:57.229 --> 14:58.772
I don't think they like me at all.

15:00.149 --> 15:01.692
They like you quite a lot, I'd say.

15:01.775 --> 15:03.193
I worry what they'll think.

15:04.320 --> 15:05.779
Besides, everybody in the hospital could

15:05.863 --> 15:06.989
get the wrong idea about us.

15:07.865 --> 15:10.910
I'm worried that because of the
mistakes I make on the daily…

15:11.702 --> 15:14.622
they'll begin to think I've
gotten distracted by "love".

15:19.585 --> 15:21.754
Whatever,
I don't care what people think about me.

15:22.796 --> 15:24.173
But I don't want you to get hurt.

15:28.218 --> 15:29.094
You're my Oppa.

15:32.014 --> 15:32.806
Sorry?

15:34.141 --> 15:34.975
What?

15:36.352 --> 15:37.227
Boyfriend

15:37.311 --> 15:38.395
You are, aren't you?

15:39.021 --> 15:39.939
You're my Oppa.

15:43.150 --> 15:45.486
Well, I suppose so,
sure, I mean, yeah, sort of, 'cause-

15:45.569 --> 15:47.071
-you're younger.
-Hey…

15:47.571 --> 15:48.739
act more casual.

15:49.615 --> 15:50.658
Cuz we're a couple.

15:55.204 --> 15:56.664
Ugh, I can't yet, it's too soon.

15:56.747 --> 15:59.917
Hey you always say Doctor Oh at work
so call me by my name instead.

16:00.000 --> 16:00.960
You're right.

16:01.919 --> 16:03.212
Alright, how about, uh-

16:04.171 --> 16:05.005
Well-

16:05.589 --> 16:06.423
Yi-

16:14.723 --> 16:15.474
Oh Yi-young.

16:17.935 --> 16:20.229
Doctor Oh!
I can't do it yet, I just can't!

16:22.314 --> 16:23.524
Let's just go home, then,

16:23.607 --> 16:24.441
Doctor Ku Do-won.

16:25.150 --> 16:25.943
Gosh.

16:31.323 --> 16:34.076
Okay,
I think that's probably enough, right?

16:34.576 --> 16:36.120
You know how she eats…

16:38.455 --> 16:39.581
Okay then do it properly.

16:39.665 --> 16:40.499
Hey.

16:41.000 --> 16:42.626
-What?
-You dating or what?

16:43.961 --> 16:44.586
Dating?

16:46.171 --> 16:47.256
What makes

16:47.339 --> 16:48.257
you say that?

16:53.345 --> 16:53.929
I am.

16:54.596 --> 16:55.222
-What?
-Huh?

16:55.305 --> 16:55.723
Sorry?

16:55.806 --> 16:56.223
Wow!

16:56.724 --> 16:57.766
Ugh, see? I totally knew it!

16:57.850 --> 17:00.894
You've had your phone in your hand
for the past twenty four hours.

17:00.978 --> 17:03.522
Either sit down like normal
or get out of here already.

17:03.605 --> 17:04.148
Who is it?

17:05.774 --> 17:06.942
Someone at the hospital?

17:08.193 --> 17:08.819
Oh!

17:09.319 --> 17:10.487
Did you already know, Do-won?

17:10.571 --> 17:11.613
Huh? Mm, sorry?

17:12.114 --> 17:12.990
What? Uh-

17:13.073 --> 17:14.074
-He didn't know about it.
-Uh-

17:14.158 --> 17:15.909
He's completely clueless about this stuff.

17:15.993 --> 17:16.577
So who is it?

17:17.161 --> 17:18.579
Oh, whatever,
never mind, just don't date anybody!

17:18.662 --> 17:20.622
-Why not?
-Sorry?

17:21.999 --> 17:22.958
Well, obviously,

17:23.042 --> 17:25.002
it's some hospital co-worker of hers,
right?

17:25.085 --> 17:27.838
I don't want her dating someone,
breaking up and creating

17:27.921 --> 17:28.589
drama for everyone.

17:29.089 --> 17:30.883
She's as fickle as the wind,
I'm telling you.

17:31.383 --> 17:35.095
She falls in and out of love so fast
you get whiplash trying to track it.

17:35.888 --> 17:36.930
That's not true.

17:37.014 --> 17:39.308
Actually,
I've never had a boyfriend before.

17:39.892 --> 17:40.893
This is my first love.

17:40.976 --> 17:41.810
Oh, please

17:43.520 --> 17:44.063
Won-u,

17:44.563 --> 17:45.355
Sang-min, and-

17:45.439 --> 17:46.565
Who was it?

17:46.648 --> 17:47.483
What was his name?

17:47.983 --> 17:49.610
Huni-huni? Is that it?

17:50.194 --> 17:53.113
Wait, no, it was something like Soni-soni,
or- Don't you remember?

17:53.697 --> 17:54.281
No,

17:54.782 --> 17:55.616
first I'm hearing it.

17:55.699 --> 17:57.034
I don't know who they are.

17:57.117 --> 17:57.993
The point is,

17:58.077 --> 18:00.579
you shouldn't run around the hospital
dating people and making your

18:00.662 --> 18:01.747
coworkers uncomfortable.

18:01.830 --> 18:03.999
You'll work with them for another
four years, at least.

18:04.083 --> 18:05.793
That's right,
that's why you should always

18:05.876 --> 18:08.253
avoid dating in the office,
or friends-to-lovers things,

18:08.337 --> 18:09.963
it's all too hard to navigate, right?

18:10.756 --> 18:12.174
Your romance started in the office.

18:12.257 --> 18:14.802
Well, if you're going to get
married like us, it's okay.

18:14.885 --> 18:15.928
I will, then.

18:16.011 --> 18:16.762
Oh, oh my God!

18:18.347 --> 18:20.891
Bro, do I look like an exotic
plant that needs watering?

18:20.974 --> 18:22.101
This is so gross, ugh.

18:22.893 --> 18:24.353
Ugh, anyway, w- what did you say?

18:24.436 --> 18:25.229
Get married?!

18:25.729 --> 18:27.439
You're gonna… You are.

18:29.691 --> 18:30.400
Ugh, Christ.

18:30.901 --> 18:33.987
Well, I'll be at the hospital before long,
tell him to come and say hello, then.

18:34.071 --> 18:35.405
We better get introduced soon.

18:42.454 --> 18:43.956
Hey, I was just kidding around.

18:44.039 --> 18:44.873
Looks like I got you.

18:45.457 --> 18:46.458
Ugh, are you serious?

18:47.042 --> 18:47.876
Hey,

18:48.502 --> 18:50.671
don't mess around about a thing like that,
you got it?

18:50.754 --> 18:53.632
-Why are you yelling right now?
-Hey, I wasn't yelling!

18:55.384 --> 18:56.385
Ugh, jeez.

18:56.885 --> 18:58.512
Those beansprouts get treated
nicer than I do!

18:58.595 --> 19:00.180
Ugh, what's wrong with her, anyway?

19:00.764 --> 19:01.849
Don't take it to heart.

19:01.932 --> 19:04.059
She's upset there's one
more blood sample still.

19:04.143 --> 19:05.227
They take it in two days.

19:05.310 --> 19:06.395
What do you mean?

19:06.478 --> 19:07.521
I'm not upset at all.

19:08.230 --> 19:09.273
Not like it matters now.

19:10.858 --> 19:14.194
The first blood sample they tested
as ambiguous, so I took a second.

19:14.278 --> 19:15.821
That was ambiguous, too.

19:16.321 --> 19:17.698
The next sample has to,

19:17.781 --> 19:19.324
double the levels of the second.

19:19.408 --> 19:20.284
There's no chance.

19:20.868 --> 19:21.493
Still, you've,

19:21.994 --> 19:23.287
had two lines in all your
pregnancy tests so far.

19:23.370 --> 19:26.498
That happened in the third IVF round,
and that didn't work out.

19:27.040 --> 19:28.041
Don't get too hopeful.

19:28.125 --> 19:29.501
I won't, I'll do like you say.

19:29.585 --> 19:30.169
Oh, well,

19:30.669 --> 19:31.545
one more chance. I mean-

19:31.628 --> 19:32.296
Well,

19:32.796 --> 19:34.464
if it happens,
then good. We'll be fine no matter what.

19:34.548 --> 19:35.132
Yeah.

19:35.632 --> 19:36.466
Oh, um,

19:36.550 --> 19:39.136
I can't go to the hospital with her then,
could one of you maybe go instead?

19:39.219 --> 19:40.053
It'd mean so much.

19:40.637 --> 19:41.555
I'll see if I can make it.

19:41.638 --> 19:43.265
That's unlike you, you must be busy.

19:43.849 --> 19:44.474
Oh.

19:44.975 --> 19:46.560
The nanoparticles project
he's on is going strong,

19:46.643 --> 19:48.937
he's achieved deterministic
statistical optimization.

19:49.021 --> 19:49.646
What?

19:50.147 --> 19:51.315
What does what again?

19:51.398 --> 19:52.232
You take nanoparticles,

19:52.316 --> 19:55.319
you layer a polymer coating on the
surface in order to modify the- Ugh,

19:55.402 --> 19:56.361
don't bother asking, now.

19:57.237 --> 19:58.989
Do you know who kicked off the research?

19:59.573 --> 20:00.282
My senior,

20:00.782 --> 20:02.576
Oh Joo-young,
who's the best researcher they had there.

20:02.659 --> 20:03.285
Gosh,

20:03.785 --> 20:04.828
that project was everything,

20:04.912 --> 20:08.957
I was in charge of the whole thing while
I was still working there, until I quit.

20:11.752 --> 20:13.253
See how far it's gotten since?

20:14.421 --> 20:15.339
What am I doing, now?

20:19.343 --> 20:21.261
Ah, that's not it, sorry, I was saying,

20:21.762 --> 20:23.513
since my hard work went into it earlier,

20:24.014 --> 20:26.058
you should work hard and give it your all.

20:26.141 --> 20:26.808
Of course.

20:27.309 --> 20:29.144
Everything will work out for us, alright?

20:30.145 --> 20:31.939
I said don't get hopeful, didn't I?

20:32.022 --> 20:33.106
Yeah, alright.

20:45.535 --> 20:46.703
-Oh, I'll take that.
-I'll take that, I'll take that,

20:46.787 --> 20:47.704
I'll take that.

20:47.788 --> 20:49.623
-Professor Seo has a patient-
-Oh, just be quiet.

20:49.706 --> 20:50.374
Uh,

20:50.874 --> 20:52.292
-Professor Kong has a patient that-
-Keep it down, would you?

20:52.376 --> 20:53.252
You'll wake the babies.

20:56.213 --> 20:58.131
I don't care either way,
so why don't you two come to

20:58.215 --> 20:59.299
an agreement and let me know?

21:01.385 --> 21:02.886
They're always arguing, jeez.

21:06.390 --> 21:09.393
Na Hyo-jin is at thirty three weeks
in the MFICU with preeclampsia.

21:10.269 --> 21:11.645
Her BP has been stable so far,

21:11.728 --> 21:15.607
but it spiked to over a hundred and fifty
this morning, and she also has a headache.

21:15.691 --> 21:16.858
The baby's coming out today.

21:17.442 --> 21:20.112
Chae Yu-ra is at thirty three
weeks in the MFICU with PPROM.

21:20.195 --> 21:21.947
She's had a fever since this morning.

21:22.030 --> 21:23.865
Her baby needs to come out today,
but its EBW is only nineteen

21:23.949 --> 21:24.866
hundred grams.

21:24.950 --> 21:26.034
Oh, really?

21:26.118 --> 21:27.369
Ours is only eighteen hundred grams.

21:27.452 --> 21:28.328
The baby's smaller,

21:28.412 --> 21:29.371
and even more fragile.

21:29.871 --> 21:31.331
My patient is suspected
to have chorioamnionitis.

21:31.415 --> 21:33.166
My patient could end up with more issues.

21:33.250 --> 21:34.501
Come on, transfer
yours to another hospital.

21:34.584 --> 21:35.460
I already said no.

21:35.544 --> 21:36.545
I can't do it either.

21:36.628 --> 21:37.838
-Hello, Pediatrics.
-Ggong says if I transfer out this

21:37.921 --> 21:39.339
-patient, I might as well leave with her.
-Yes, alright, I'll be right there.

21:39.423 --> 21:40.507
Guess you better leave, then.

21:40.590 --> 21:42.426
I'm not going anywhere
without that incubator.

21:42.509 --> 21:43.552
What're you doing?

21:43.635 --> 21:44.636
Where're you going?

21:44.720 --> 21:47.347
Doctor Myeong's doing a delivery and
says the baby isn't doing well.

21:47.431 --> 21:48.015
Move, please.

21:48.598 --> 21:49.349
Thanks.

21:50.559 --> 21:51.601
Hey, watch your feet.

21:56.106 --> 21:58.525
Ugh, he just stole that
right out from under us!

22:00.944 --> 22:02.779
You need to come fix this right away.

22:03.697 --> 22:04.698
See, my mother's IV,

22:05.490 --> 22:06.575
is leaking some more.

22:06.658 --> 22:07.284
Ah,

22:07.784 --> 22:08.994
alright, I'll come check.

22:09.953 --> 22:10.871
I'd appreciate it.

22:17.627 --> 22:18.420
Isn't that the guy,

22:18.920 --> 22:21.840
who kept on making threats just because
it took someone two tries in order to

22:21.923 --> 22:22.841
place his mother's IV?

22:22.924 --> 22:24.009
That's him all right.

22:24.092 --> 22:26.094
He said "thank you"?
I'm surprised he didn't yell again.

22:26.178 --> 22:26.762
Ah,

22:27.262 --> 22:28.221
well, the other day,

22:28.305 --> 22:31.183
the professor may have gotten angry when
they heard him refer to me as "girl",

22:31.266 --> 22:33.310
so I'd assume that's probably
why he changed.

22:33.810 --> 22:36.605
It's just the tone of his voice,
otherwise he's been nice.

22:36.688 --> 22:37.689
Well, I better take a look.

22:37.773 --> 22:38.690
Alright.

22:41.109 --> 22:44.196
Hey, why aren't you doing anything
about the patient who has a fever?

22:44.279 --> 22:45.113
Oh,

22:45.781 --> 22:46.615
oh no, that's-

22:47.157 --> 22:49.409
I did a chest x-ray,
which showed nothing out of the ordinary,

22:49.493 --> 22:51.411
and since she's only on POD one,
I've been observing.

22:51.495 --> 22:53.914
Even with a completely normal x-ray,
if a fever crops up,

22:53.997 --> 22:55.665
you should be taking action to handle it.

22:55.749 --> 22:58.168
Blood and urine cultures aren't
done until POD two to three,

22:58.251 --> 22:59.920
so it would be too early to run those,

23:00.420 --> 23:03.632
And a wound culture on POD four or five
is only warranted if the fever has

23:03.715 --> 23:04.674
continued that long.

23:05.842 --> 23:07.594
I'll be checking the wound
during the routine

23:07.677 --> 23:09.262
dressing change tomorrow to be sure.

23:09.346 --> 23:10.180
Hey,

23:10.847 --> 23:11.932
you teaching me right now?

23:12.599 --> 23:13.225
No.

23:13.725 --> 23:14.601
Didn't I tell you?

23:15.102 --> 23:17.187
Whenever I already know something,
don't tell me about it like it's news.

23:17.270 --> 23:20.565
I don't need a list of factoids
that I'm familiar with already!

23:21.942 --> 23:22.984
Sorry about that.

23:23.068 --> 23:25.570
Regardless of what POD it is,
if the patient has a fever,

23:25.654 --> 23:27.656
don't you think you need to find out why?

23:27.739 --> 23:28.949
How would you do that?

23:32.536 --> 23:33.662
Don't know?

23:33.745 --> 23:36.081
-No, I know.
-Hurry up and answer me, then!

23:38.041 --> 23:40.627
You just told me I can't explain
something you already know.

23:42.462 --> 23:44.381
Seriously?
Do you think this is all a joke?

23:47.801 --> 23:50.470
Blood cultures, urine cultures,
or just checking for wound complications,

23:50.554 --> 23:51.471
I don't really care,

23:51.555 --> 23:52.681
just resolve the issue.

23:53.432 --> 23:54.599
Fever workup, get on it.

23:54.683 --> 23:55.767
Go do that immediately.

23:55.851 --> 23:58.186
-You understand?
-I understand, Professor.

24:01.231 --> 24:02.482
If this was for Obstetrics,

24:02.566 --> 24:04.067
you'd take the work seriously.

24:10.031 --> 24:10.866
Ouch!

24:11.450 --> 24:13.201
Why'd he bring Obstetrics into this?

24:13.285 --> 24:14.286
No idea.

24:14.369 --> 24:17.456
Last time he said I did too many tests
on POD one, but he's still angry at me.

24:17.539 --> 24:18.665
I'm totally confused, now.

24:20.125 --> 24:21.042
It seems like he's,

24:21.626 --> 24:22.335
totally,

24:22.836 --> 24:24.254
out to get you right now.

24:25.630 --> 24:26.631
You upset him, didn't you?

24:27.591 --> 24:28.425
Did I?

24:29.634 --> 24:30.260
No,

24:30.760 --> 24:31.803
nothing happened.

24:32.387 --> 24:33.221
Mm.

24:33.847 --> 24:34.681
Sa-bi,

24:35.724 --> 24:37.934
why don't I let you in
on my personal tactic.

24:38.727 --> 24:39.895
Say a professor is upset

24:39.978 --> 24:40.562
or…

24:41.062 --> 24:42.022
unhappy.

24:42.105 --> 24:43.648
What are you supposed to do?

24:43.732 --> 24:46.318
At times like that,
you just say, "I apologize!"

24:46.818 --> 24:48.528
Why apologize for
something if I'm not at fault?

24:48.612 --> 24:49.571
Just try it!

24:50.071 --> 24:51.865
Just act like it's your
fault and say you're sorry!

24:51.948 --> 24:53.492
How, if I didn't make a mistake, though?

24:53.575 --> 24:54.743
Hang on, that's not the-

24:56.620 --> 24:57.204
Ugh.

24:58.288 --> 24:59.206
It's alright. Mm.

25:00.123 --> 25:01.333
Just do what's best for you.

25:03.168 --> 25:04.002
I gotta go to surgery.

25:04.503 --> 25:05.462
So as for you, Sa-Bi,

25:05.962 --> 25:07.339
stay out of trouble with everyone.

25:07.422 --> 25:08.256
Gosh.

25:10.467 --> 25:12.469
You know, I can't believe we're here.

25:13.261 --> 25:15.055
I'm finally giving advice like this.

25:37.452 --> 25:38.370
Can I ask, Professor?

25:38.954 --> 25:41.831
Why are you doing surgery this
way instead of opening her up?

25:43.166 --> 25:44.000
Oh,

25:44.543 --> 25:45.794
I'm not saying there's
anything wrong with it.

25:45.877 --> 25:46.836
It's just that,

25:47.420 --> 25:48.171
this is a complicated surgery,

25:48.255 --> 25:50.799
so I wondered why you did a laparoscopy
instead of a laparotomy.

25:50.882 --> 25:51.675
That's all I meant.

25:52.259 --> 25:54.636
I'm not challenging you,
it's a genuine question.

25:54.719 --> 25:55.637
It really is.

25:58.807 --> 26:00.642
Wow, I'm so touched by your curiosity.

26:01.142 --> 26:02.143
Honestly,

26:02.227 --> 26:04.938
I think this is the first time ever during
a surgery that an R One has asked me

26:05.021 --> 26:05.939
a question.

26:06.856 --> 26:07.691
Whoa.

26:13.446 --> 26:14.698
Everyone else just goes,

26:15.574 --> 26:18.577
I assume this is right,
the professor must know what he's doing.

26:18.660 --> 26:21.329
Nobody gets curious enough to
ask about sometihng like this,

26:21.413 --> 26:22.914
especially during the surgery itself.

26:23.415 --> 26:24.374
Hm!

26:26.334 --> 26:27.836
According to the all the current research,

26:27.919 --> 26:29.921
there is actually no
difference in outcome,

26:30.005 --> 26:32.841
between a laparoscopy and a laparotomy,
so either works.

26:33.466 --> 26:34.384
But today,

26:34.467 --> 26:36.553
we're considering the case
of this particular patient,

26:36.636 --> 26:37.804
and she's advanced in years.

26:38.305 --> 26:40.098
So for the patient's benefit, my aim,

26:40.181 --> 26:41.266
was to reduce surgery time,

26:41.766 --> 26:43.226
as much as I possibly could.

26:43.977 --> 26:44.811
So then, have I,

26:45.312 --> 26:46.646
answered your question at all,

26:47.147 --> 26:48.231
uh,

26:48.315 --> 26:49.566
Doctor Yoon Tae-jin?

26:50.191 --> 26:51.192
Um Jae-il, actually.

26:51.276 --> 26:52.902
Oh, yes, yes,
yes. That's right, that's right,

26:52.986 --> 26:54.529
Um Jae-il, Um Jae-il. Yes, i know.

26:54.613 --> 26:56.990
Of course,
I know, he's, uh, you know, the, uh,

26:57.073 --> 26:57.741
the,

26:58.241 --> 26:59.826
H- H- H- H- Hi Man.

26:59.909 --> 27:00.910
Hi-Boyz.

27:02.037 --> 27:02.787
Sorry.

27:03.288 --> 27:03.872
Sorry

27:04.372 --> 27:05.415
Boy.

27:07.000 --> 27:08.168
Specimen coming out now.

27:10.003 --> 27:11.087
Goodness.

27:13.632 --> 27:15.008
Just look at this thing here.

27:15.717 --> 27:19.095
Why does a terrible thing like this
have to form in the first place?

27:19.179 --> 27:20.180
It's so unfortunate.

27:21.806 --> 27:23.391
Creates such anguish and pain.

27:24.142 --> 27:25.060
Goodness.

27:26.394 --> 27:27.270
Anyway,

27:29.022 --> 27:29.856
Hi-Boyz.

27:37.656 --> 27:38.740
You're really not going?

27:38.823 --> 27:40.575
Professor Kong getting
us pizza is actually

27:40.659 --> 27:41.993
a very rare event, you know?

27:42.077 --> 27:44.496
And it's from someplace really good,
I heard.

27:45.872 --> 27:46.873
No thanks.

27:46.956 --> 27:48.541
I don't like pizza, so you go ahead.

27:48.625 --> 27:49.626
You told me

27:49.709 --> 27:50.543
you like pizza.

27:50.627 --> 27:51.211
So…

27:51.711 --> 27:52.629
Ah.

27:54.464 --> 27:55.590
I do like pizza.

27:55.674 --> 27:56.758
Just not today.

27:57.717 --> 27:58.343
Indigestion.

27:58.843 --> 28:00.720
-Oh, I can get you-
-No don't do that!

28:02.347 --> 28:03.181
Don't worry about it.

28:03.264 --> 28:04.391
I don't want medication.

28:05.392 --> 28:06.142
You guys go ahead.

28:06.226 --> 28:08.311
-We'll grab a bite and be really quick!
-No need to.

28:08.395 --> 28:09.396
Why not?

28:12.148 --> 28:13.233
There's no rush, have fun.

28:14.234 --> 28:15.110
Go and eat a lot,

28:15.193 --> 28:16.152
and chew thoroughly,

28:16.653 --> 28:18.113
or you could get indigestion.

28:19.030 --> 28:19.572
I see.

28:20.240 --> 28:21.157
-Okay,
-Okay, we'll get some pizza, then.

28:21.241 --> 28:21.866
See you later.

28:22.450 --> 28:23.451
Ooh, I'm so excited!

28:40.301 --> 28:42.220
You could've had pizza first, you know?

28:44.180 --> 28:45.223
I'd rather have this.

29:13.209 --> 29:14.252
Well, Doctor Oh,

29:15.670 --> 29:17.422
I feel just a little confused right now.

29:17.505 --> 29:20.341
Do you wanna keep this under wraps
or shout it from the rooftop?

29:21.301 --> 29:22.051
I don't know yet.

29:24.304 --> 29:25.889
But I really want to be with you.

29:25.972 --> 29:26.931
I know that much.

29:31.770 --> 29:32.437
Me too.

29:49.746 --> 29:51.080
Think you can help out a little?

29:57.170 --> 29:57.754
Pork, too.

29:58.254 --> 29:59.214
-Pork?
-Mm-hm.

30:01.966 --> 30:03.092
-And spinach?
-Oh, and spinach?

30:03.176 --> 30:04.010
Mm-hm.

30:08.973 --> 30:11.601
I'm so tired right now I can't
lift the spoon up that high.

30:12.101 --> 30:14.312
-Well, I can handle that.
-No, Doctor Oh, it's alright-

30:14.395 --> 30:16.648
-Hey, I'm strong.
-Oh, you really don't have to do that.

30:16.731 --> 30:17.565
Ah.

30:19.776 --> 30:20.485
Ah.

30:23.363 --> 30:24.906
Ugh, hey! If you drop my chopsticks,

30:25.406 --> 30:26.908
you should at least pick them-

30:27.492 --> 30:28.159
Oh,

30:28.660 --> 30:30.411
Myeong Eun-won. Hi, Doctor.

30:30.495 --> 30:31.162
Mm?

30:31.663 --> 30:33.164
-Oh, Doctor Oh.
-Yes?

30:33.248 --> 30:36.459
The surgery ahead of us is running long,
so hold the patient maybe half an hour.

30:36.543 --> 30:37.001
Alright.

30:42.507 --> 30:43.299
Hello, Professor.

30:44.634 --> 30:47.470
Professor Kong wrote a letter of
recommendation for me already.

30:47.971 --> 30:50.181
The application deadline for
professorships is next week,

30:50.265 --> 30:52.475
I'm going to touch mine
up before submission.

30:53.351 --> 30:53.977
Yes.

30:54.477 --> 30:56.020
I appreciate you.

31:02.068 --> 31:03.236
Oh hey, Doctor Ku.

31:04.195 --> 31:05.071
Have you heard

31:05.154 --> 31:08.116
about how many people have applied
for professorships this year?

31:08.700 --> 31:09.534
I haven't.

31:10.159 --> 31:12.412
Ah, Doctor Yoo Jeong-hye is applying,
I heard about that.

31:12.495 --> 31:13.079
Ah,

31:13.580 --> 31:14.622
she is?

31:16.082 --> 31:16.749
Hey,

31:17.250 --> 31:18.793
are you going to eat that? Can I-

31:20.545 --> 31:21.379
Mm.

31:22.338 --> 31:23.214
I had better go.

31:24.048 --> 31:25.884
-Enjoy lunch.
-Bye.

31:33.057 --> 31:33.975
That was close.

31:35.059 --> 31:37.812
How can a hospital as large
as this not have any privacy?

31:37.896 --> 31:38.980
How can we date at work?

31:39.063 --> 31:40.481
Well, dates aren't
supposed to go on at work, really.

31:40.565 --> 31:42.775
All the free time we have is spent at
work, how else are we supposed to date?

31:42.859 --> 31:44.027
How else do we go on a date?

31:44.986 --> 31:45.653
And at home,

31:46.154 --> 31:47.780
there's always two pairs of eyes watching.

31:48.573 --> 31:49.490
Yeah, you're right.

31:50.199 --> 31:52.118
And I gotta put in time
here over the weekend.

31:52.201 --> 31:53.036
Really?

31:54.454 --> 31:55.371
Let's meet up tonight.

31:55.455 --> 31:56.414
By the fire escape.

31:56.497 --> 31:57.999
-Those stairs shoud be empty-
-Mm-mm.

31:58.082 --> 31:59.459
Someone grabbed up every floor.

32:00.043 --> 32:01.586
Does anyone here actually work?

32:04.172 --> 32:05.214
There's the elevator.

32:06.633 --> 32:08.343
Doctor Oh, that's only on TV,
how would that actually work?

32:08.426 --> 32:09.928
I want to see you.

32:11.262 --> 32:11.971
Uh,

32:12.472 --> 32:14.807
I'll have about half an hour after nine
and we can go and get a coffee together,

32:14.891 --> 32:15.558
okay?

32:16.059 --> 32:17.685
-It'll be just us.
-You gotta deal.

32:18.686 --> 32:19.520
We'll go to the-

32:20.897 --> 32:22.315
PYO NAM-KYUNG

32:22.815 --> 32:23.483
Ugh,

32:23.983 --> 32:25.568
this is the absolute worse timing.

32:26.361 --> 32:27.195
What?

32:31.783 --> 32:35.244
Ma'am, your cervical length is fine,
and everything's looking really good.

32:35.328 --> 32:37.538
You can go back to the ward now,
I'm all done here.

32:37.622 --> 32:38.998
Thanks so much, I'm really glad.

32:39.082 --> 32:40.833
I need to start outpatient ultrasounds.

32:40.917 --> 32:41.918
Please hurry.

32:42.001 --> 32:44.212
-Just one more, please? It'll be my last!
-No, you can't.

32:44.295 --> 32:46.255
-Patients are waiting outside.
-But I'm fast!

32:46.339 --> 32:47.215
I said you can't.

32:47.298 --> 32:49.258
Your patient's upstairs,
so bring the portable machine to her.

32:49.342 --> 32:51.594
-Why clog up things down here?
-Professor Kong told me it's best

32:51.678 --> 32:52.762
that I use the machine in here.

32:52.845 --> 32:54.222
That seems like a you issue.

32:57.350 --> 32:58.393
Oh, sorry about that.

32:59.519 --> 33:00.436
Let's go.

33:07.819 --> 33:09.737
The outpatient appointments are behind,
now.

33:09.821 --> 33:12.156
Look,
I really do understand all that, I get it.

33:12.240 --> 33:14.701
I'm doing all the Doppler scans here
'cause Ggong is making really

33:14.784 --> 33:17.370
important decisions and told
me to use this machine.

33:19.205 --> 33:19.914
Ah.

33:19.998 --> 33:20.832
Be there in a sec.

33:20.915 --> 33:22.917
Please return to your seat, Miss, and

33:23.001 --> 33:24.460
I can help you in a minute or two.

33:24.961 --> 33:25.878
Sure.

33:27.630 --> 33:30.133
Well, you missed your chance,
outpatient appointments stop at lunch.

33:30.216 --> 33:32.301
Yeah, but it got
sprung on me after lunch!

33:33.302 --> 33:35.388
Can't you help me out just this once,
c'mon…

33:35.471 --> 33:38.516
-I'll be super quick, I promise.
-Seriously…

33:39.475 --> 33:40.393
Fine be quick.

33:42.103 --> 33:42.979
Yes, Professor?

33:43.062 --> 33:45.023
Where's Miss Moon Cha-seon's ultrasound?

33:45.106 --> 33:46.858
Why isn't she ready for her consultation?

33:46.941 --> 33:49.235
Oh, sorry about that,
things are backed up down here.

33:49.318 --> 33:51.154
Just give me a minute,
I'll get everything done.

33:51.237 --> 33:52.113
Oh Yi-young,

33:52.196 --> 33:55.033
the ultrasounds have been holding
up my appointments all morning.

33:55.116 --> 33:56.451
Do I need to come there myself?

33:56.534 --> 33:57.952
No don't come, I'm on it!

33:58.786 --> 33:59.787
Gimme just a minute!

34:06.210 --> 34:06.794
Yes, Professor?

34:07.295 --> 34:08.296
Uh,

34:08.379 --> 34:09.714
I completed the ultrasounds.

34:10.298 --> 34:12.967
Well, except there's just this
one patient I couldn't-

34:14.469 --> 34:15.386
Of course,

34:15.470 --> 34:16.345
I'm on it.

34:16.429 --> 34:17.263
Yes.

34:17.805 --> 34:19.849
Yeah, just a minute, I'll get it done.

34:22.602 --> 34:23.561
Hey, Oh Yi-young,

34:23.644 --> 34:24.645
let me finish!

34:25.229 --> 34:25.855
Hello.

34:26.355 --> 34:27.398
-Hello.
-Hello.

34:28.357 --> 34:29.650
-Hello.
-Hello, Professor.

34:30.526 --> 34:31.152
Hello.

34:31.652 --> 34:32.737
-Hello.
-Oops, here!

34:32.820 --> 34:33.654
Ugh,

34:34.155 --> 34:35.698
if they could just be more responsible
and actually plan,

34:35.782 --> 34:37.617
there'd be no need to run around now.

34:38.785 --> 34:39.869
Sorry we were running late.

34:40.369 --> 34:41.496
Let me take a look a this.

34:41.996 --> 34:43.081
Oh, oh!

34:43.164 --> 34:44.874
Whoa! Hey, stop! What are you doing?

34:45.458 --> 34:46.584
Ah, ah, that's hot!

34:46.667 --> 34:47.502
Ah!

35:00.181 --> 35:02.308
Jeon Mi-yeon's surgery is
first thing in the morning.

35:02.391 --> 35:05.311
An ostomy for intestinal obstruction;
aren't you aware of that?

35:05.895 --> 35:06.437
I'm aware.

35:06.938 --> 35:07.772
Then why,

35:07.855 --> 35:09.732
was there porridge on her table
when I ordered a fast for her?

35:09.816 --> 35:12.193
Were you trying to sabotage
the surgery or what?

35:13.277 --> 35:13.945
That's not-

35:14.445 --> 35:17.532
And the Surgeon-in-Chief of the department
is doing the surgery since I requested it.

35:17.615 --> 35:20.868
If it's cancelled because of it,
can you imagine how stupid I'd look then?

35:21.369 --> 35:22.578
Uh-

35:23.246 --> 35:24.122
It's co-

35:24.205 --> 35:25.331
managed,

35:25.414 --> 35:26.874
with the surgery team, so…

35:26.958 --> 35:27.917
What happened?

35:28.501 --> 35:29.710
Well, what about it? Go on.

35:30.711 --> 35:32.004
Apparently their resident,

35:33.047 --> 35:33.923
was the one

35:34.006 --> 35:35.049
who entered--

35:35.133 --> 35:35.800
They did what?

35:37.009 --> 35:38.386
Just say something already!

35:39.720 --> 35:40.638
I'm sorry.

35:40.721 --> 35:41.639
Tell me,

35:42.140 --> 35:45.852
do you come here to help patients,
or are you just trying to kill old ladies?

35:46.435 --> 35:49.981
Thank God I was there doing my rounds,
or it would have been a complete disaster.

35:50.064 --> 35:50.773
Oh, Professor Jo!

35:51.274 --> 35:52.483
There you are, gosh.

35:52.567 --> 35:53.526
Oh, Professor.

35:54.110 --> 35:56.320
-Why aren't you answering your phone?
-Oh-

35:56.821 --> 35:59.073
Oh! Oh no,
I'm sorry, I'm so sorry, I just-

35:59.157 --> 36:00.074
I was,

36:00.158 --> 36:01.450
dealing with my resident. So,

36:01.534 --> 36:02.743
may I assist with anything?

36:02.827 --> 36:03.786
I'm afraid so.

36:04.871 --> 36:06.664
One of our residents entered
an order wrong.

36:07.290 --> 36:09.333
He ordered a meal for Miss Jeon Mi-yeon

36:09.417 --> 36:11.460
He confused her with someone else,
I guess.

36:11.544 --> 36:13.171
Ah-ha, you- you're saying that

36:13.254 --> 36:14.130
he cleared her to eat?

36:14.630 --> 36:16.132
Ah, I see,
yeah. So- so that would explain

36:16.215 --> 36:17.508
porridge getting sent to her.

36:17.592 --> 36:18.342
That's right.

36:18.426 --> 36:19.302
Well, has she…

36:19.385 --> 36:20.803
already eaten the porridge?

36:21.304 --> 36:22.346
No, she didn't eat it.

36:22.430 --> 36:23.431
Ah, thank goodness.

36:23.514 --> 36:26.601
You don't need to worry about things
like that, I double-check everything just

36:26.684 --> 36:28.019
-in case.
-What a relief this is.

36:28.519 --> 36:30.021
Now apologize to the Doctor.

36:31.480 --> 36:32.523
I really am sorry.

36:35.776 --> 36:36.777
I'm sorry about that.

36:37.361 --> 36:38.070
It's alright.

36:38.571 --> 36:40.031
So just try not to worry now, okay?

36:40.114 --> 36:41.616
These things do happen, right?

36:42.241 --> 36:43.868
You should be more careful going forward.

36:43.951 --> 36:44.660
I will.

36:45.161 --> 36:47.496
Oh, and, uh, Professor,
since you're here, how does tea sound?

36:47.580 --> 36:48.414
That sounds great.

36:48.497 --> 36:49.540
Tea it is.

36:49.624 --> 36:50.917
-Great.
-Get back to work.

36:52.793 --> 36:53.461
Ah, gosh.

36:53.961 --> 36:55.213
How are you?

37:15.691 --> 37:16.776
I'm a little confused,

37:18.986 --> 37:20.488
why you didn't tell him earlier.

37:22.448 --> 37:23.699
I was just too scared.

37:26.786 --> 37:28.454
Just know he made the mistake, not you.

37:29.288 --> 37:30.623
You didn't do anything wrong.

37:31.123 --> 37:32.708
Hold your head up high, okay?

37:34.794 --> 37:35.378
Right.

37:35.878 --> 37:36.921
Just stay strong.

37:38.381 --> 37:39.215
Don't let it-

37:42.343 --> 37:43.552
Ah, words won't help right now.

37:45.346 --> 37:47.807
Since there are plenty of
better ways to set things right.

37:47.890 --> 37:48.516
Oh,

37:49.016 --> 37:50.810
don't, I'm alright. I appreciate it.

37:51.894 --> 37:54.313
I can enter that medication order for you,
go on.

37:54.897 --> 37:56.315
Go get a cup of coffee, okay?

37:56.857 --> 37:57.942
No, I'm fine.

37:58.025 --> 37:58.901
Hang on, hang on.

37:59.402 --> 38:01.404
I insist, it's actually- well,
it's because I'm thirsty.

38:01.487 --> 38:02.863
Right, come on, go, go, go.

38:02.947 --> 38:04.740
Let's go,
get up, get up, come on, just go.

38:04.824 --> 38:06.033
Go on. Good,

38:06.117 --> 38:07.118
now get going.

38:07.660 --> 38:08.369
Uh, for me, uh,

38:08.869 --> 38:10.288
an iced americano sounds really good,

38:10.371 --> 38:11.247
in like,

38:11.330 --> 38:12.373
a big size, huge.

38:13.040 --> 38:14.208
I mean, you know, right?

38:16.043 --> 38:18.421
Let me see,
now, huh? Just what do we have here?

38:35.771 --> 38:36.856
Anybody want some food?

38:43.195 --> 38:43.738
Do you?

38:46.490 --> 38:47.074
What?

38:47.658 --> 38:49.160
Is it your coffee? It tastes bad, or what?

38:49.243 --> 38:50.077
It's great.

38:55.916 --> 38:57.793
Pork stir-fry down in the cafeteria.

38:57.877 --> 38:58.711
Really?

38:58.794 --> 39:00.129
-Let's go.
-Hey, Um Jae-il,

39:00.212 --> 39:01.505
isn't today supposed to
be a street food day?

39:01.589 --> 39:02.882
Just ask her about that.

39:02.965 --> 39:03.632
Who do I ask?

39:04.717 --> 39:06.552
Um Jae-il, I had street food earlier-

39:06.635 --> 39:08.220
And I had stir-fry before, so.

39:11.098 --> 39:12.600
-So for dinner, then-
-Stir-fry.

39:12.683 --> 39:13.184
Street food.

39:15.978 --> 39:17.021
You two work this out.

39:17.104 --> 39:18.814
I don't want to get involved.

39:19.648 --> 39:20.191
Did you have a fight?

39:20.691 --> 39:21.525
-No way.
-No way.

39:22.109 --> 39:22.860
They so did.

39:22.943 --> 39:24.362
Not true, why would we be fighting?

39:24.445 --> 39:25.321
Exactly.

39:25.404 --> 39:26.947
There's no reason we'd be fighting.

39:27.031 --> 39:29.033
She just got me in trouble, that's all.

39:29.116 --> 39:30.201
Only returned the favor.

39:31.035 --> 39:32.411
Hey, Sa-bi,

39:32.953 --> 39:34.997
is it really such a big crime to do an
ultrasound with an inpatient who might

39:35.081 --> 39:35.790
be critical,

39:35.873 --> 39:38.167
-before the outpatient sessions?
-Hey, Um Jae-il, isn't it shocking that

39:38.250 --> 39:41.045
someone's confused about how the
outpatient process works?

39:43.172 --> 39:43.714
I was,

39:44.215 --> 39:44.882
just asking,

39:45.466 --> 39:46.926
if anybody here might want dinner.

39:50.596 --> 39:51.514
Alright, then.

39:52.556 --> 39:54.975
I suppose we'll starve,
now. Are you happy, guys?

39:56.060 --> 39:57.269
Hey! That's mine, don't!

39:57.353 --> 39:59.063
Ryu Jae-hui bought me this one!

39:59.855 --> 40:00.898
Ugh, I'm sorry!

40:03.317 --> 40:05.361
Ugh, seriously. Guys,

40:05.444 --> 40:06.737
why do you take things this far, huh?

40:06.821 --> 40:08.906
Being so angry over nothing? Seriously?

40:08.989 --> 40:09.907
Ah, jeez.

40:10.408 --> 40:11.992
I can't stay here like this.

40:13.035 --> 40:14.412
So uh uh - Don't try to stop me, guys!

40:14.495 --> 40:15.704
I really can't stay here!

40:16.330 --> 40:16.956
Ugh.

40:17.456 --> 40:18.457
Come on.

40:36.642 --> 40:37.768
Alright, you're all set.

40:37.852 --> 40:39.812
We'll be sure to call as soon
as we get the results.

40:39.895 --> 40:41.564
It'll take around an hour or so.

40:41.647 --> 40:42.481
So,

40:43.065 --> 40:44.525
there's no more blood tests,
now, am I right?

40:44.608 --> 40:46.110
This blood sample was the last one?

40:46.193 --> 40:47.403
I expect it's the last, yes.

40:47.486 --> 40:48.487
So then,

40:49.363 --> 40:50.948
what comes next in the whole process?

40:51.031 --> 40:51.866
Oh,

40:52.450 --> 40:54.577
if the levels all appear good,
you'll make an appointment

40:54.660 --> 40:55.244
for an ultrasound.

40:55.744 --> 40:58.539
You must mean the scan, right?
The womb scan thing that you guys do?

40:58.622 --> 40:59.457
Yes.

41:01.834 --> 41:03.586
And an hour from now means
you'll be calling

41:03.669 --> 41:05.004
around one thirty or so, right?

41:05.087 --> 41:07.840
I'll call you as soon as the results
come out, so don't worry.

41:07.923 --> 41:08.466
Right,

41:08.966 --> 41:10.176
I'm grateful, thanks.

41:26.233 --> 41:27.067
Oh Yi-young.

41:27.151 --> 41:30.988
Don't delay the outpatient ultrasounds
tomorrow, we have a full schedule, 'kay?

41:31.071 --> 41:32.072
Yes.

41:33.365 --> 41:34.241
That is,

41:34.325 --> 41:35.242
yes, I'm on it.

41:35.743 --> 41:37.786
Backed-up ultrasounds bring complaints
in like a flood, don't they?

41:37.870 --> 41:39.580
Pyo Nam-kyung,

41:39.663 --> 41:41.540
I have twenty five outpatients tomorrow
coming in to be scanned, right?

41:41.624 --> 41:42.500
Uh, yeah.

41:42.583 --> 41:44.710
I need to be done with everything
no later than five, then.

41:44.793 --> 41:46.504
No delays for any reason, understand?

41:46.587 --> 41:47.963
I'll get them wrapped up by then.

41:49.632 --> 41:52.635
I've heard a spot is opening in
the Obstetrics ward here soon.

41:52.718 --> 41:54.011
Yes, I'm going to take it.

41:54.929 --> 41:56.972
I was just about to say the same thing.

41:57.056 --> 41:58.140
I'll take it, lock it down.

41:58.224 --> 42:00.309
I have a patient stuck in Gynecology
that needs to transfer.

42:00.392 --> 42:01.519
Making rounds slow me down.

42:02.019 --> 42:03.646
I'm counting on you, Doctor, okay?

42:03.729 --> 42:04.730
I will.

42:06.106 --> 42:07.107
I'm in the same situation.

42:07.650 --> 42:10.444
I want my patient brought from Gynecology,
so please sort it out.

42:10.528 --> 42:11.695
But make sure you eat, too.

42:12.279 --> 42:13.155
Alright.

42:15.616 --> 42:18.744
Is this Administration? Yeah,
I'm OBGYN resident Pyo Nam-kyung, hi!

42:18.827 --> 42:19.495
Yes,

42:19.995 --> 42:21.539
I was told a bed opened
up in the Obstetrics ward.

42:21.622 --> 42:22.289
Hey!

42:31.006 --> 42:33.509
Attention, please. We would like to
remind all visitors that the visiting

42:33.592 --> 42:36.428
hours at our facility are from nine AM to
eight PM. Please ensure you've signed in

42:36.512 --> 42:39.348
at the front desk upon entering. For the
safety and comfort of all our patients, we

42:39.431 --> 42:41.809
kindly ask that you refrain from using
your mobile phones in patient care areas.

42:41.892 --> 42:44.270
-Thank you for your cooperation.
-Sorry, I had work to do.

42:44.353 --> 42:45.604
Why are you acting so weird?

42:45.688 --> 42:46.689
It doesn't suit you.

42:48.857 --> 42:49.817
Have they called you yet?

42:51.068 --> 42:51.902
No.

43:00.452 --> 43:01.078
Nervous?

43:02.162 --> 43:03.080
Not at all.

43:05.874 --> 43:07.626
If it was happening,
it'd be confirmed after

43:07.710 --> 43:08.752
the first test I did.

43:09.962 --> 43:11.046
Let's not count on it.

43:14.592 --> 43:15.217
Hello?

43:15.718 --> 43:17.094
Yes, this is Oh Joo-young.

43:19.513 --> 43:20.347
Ah.

43:22.808 --> 43:23.809
Uh-huh, I see.

43:25.519 --> 43:26.812
Yup, thanks so much, then.

43:27.855 --> 43:28.689
Uh-huh.

43:43.370 --> 43:44.413
The level's at what?

43:44.496 --> 43:45.581
Ninety one.

43:46.248 --> 43:49.627
It was one fifty three before this one,
it's much lower than it was.

43:50.544 --> 43:51.420
A chemical pregnancy?

43:53.297 --> 43:54.131
How did you know?

43:57.009 --> 43:57.885
Wait, right.

43:57.968 --> 43:59.136
You're a doctor.

44:01.889 --> 44:03.557
How can you be laughing right now?

44:05.893 --> 44:07.770
I just figured it wasn't going to work.

44:07.853 --> 44:09.063
Must explain why I'm not,

44:09.146 --> 44:11.023
so torn up this time as much as I thought.

44:14.068 --> 44:15.569
Hey, I said it's alright.

44:16.445 --> 44:19.239
I didn't hear the heartbeat,
and I didn't feel them move or anything,

44:19.323 --> 44:19.990
relax.

44:20.074 --> 44:22.242
All I've lost is a bunch of cells,
you know?

44:23.160 --> 44:23.744
I'll be fine.

44:24.328 --> 44:26.955
And anyway,
I still have two more of the embryos left.

44:27.039 --> 44:27.915
It's alright.

44:27.998 --> 44:29.667
Two more tries. Mm.

44:37.633 --> 44:38.509
Let's grab lunch.

44:39.051 --> 44:39.968
I've got some time.

44:42.137 --> 44:43.305
You must be much too busy, no.

44:44.223 --> 44:45.349
Treat me to a coffee.

44:46.850 --> 44:48.185
Since I started doing IVF again,

44:48.268 --> 44:50.187
I haven't been able to have any coffee.

44:50.854 --> 44:52.523
So a caffeine hit sounds really great.

44:55.693 --> 44:57.611
-Let's go, then.
-Mm.

45:05.536 --> 45:06.286
You?

45:07.705 --> 45:08.622
The usual.

45:09.957 --> 45:12.376
An iced americano for her,
and an iced latte as well if you could,

45:12.459 --> 45:13.919
thank you. Oh,

45:14.002 --> 45:16.004
and the iced latte is decaffeinated-

45:20.050 --> 45:20.843
Oh.

45:21.385 --> 45:22.094
No, it's good.

45:27.516 --> 45:29.309
That habit really did form quick!

45:32.896 --> 45:33.814
Ah, God.

45:35.899 --> 45:37.109
I just can't believe I tried,

45:37.609 --> 45:39.820
so hard,
and still got nothing back at all.

45:57.212 --> 45:57.963
Hey,

45:58.547 --> 45:59.465
hey, stop.

46:04.720 --> 46:07.264
Sorry 'bout that,
one iced americano regular sized.

46:16.982 --> 46:18.150
And an iced cafe latte,

46:18.233 --> 46:19.318
with an extra shot.

46:20.444 --> 46:21.445
No, two extra shots

46:21.945 --> 46:22.863
Alright.

46:44.134 --> 46:46.470
PROFESSOR JO JOON-MO

46:56.814 --> 46:57.564
Mm.

46:58.357 --> 46:59.441
Hello, Professor.

47:00.400 --> 47:02.402
Oh, Kim Sa-bi just went to the bathroom.

47:03.821 --> 47:05.864
Let me check and I'll
have her call you back.

47:06.448 --> 47:07.199
Alright.

47:10.244 --> 47:11.036
It's nothing, really.

47:11.745 --> 47:13.247
Availability check for the OR.

47:14.373 --> 47:15.207
Oh.

47:17.876 --> 47:18.836
Have you eaten?

47:20.671 --> 47:21.797
Then come to the cafeteria.

47:21.880 --> 47:22.714
What?

47:23.298 --> 47:24.383
Scared you'll meet him there?

47:27.636 --> 47:28.554
What are you doing here?

47:28.637 --> 47:30.138
What anyone else would do here.

47:30.222 --> 47:31.306
Withdraw cash.

47:38.021 --> 47:39.147
They'll be closing soon.

47:39.231 --> 47:40.148
Let's go.

47:40.732 --> 47:41.483
Mm-hm.

47:44.611 --> 47:45.904
If you just want to be alone,

47:46.405 --> 47:47.781
this place is pretty good.

47:49.366 --> 47:50.993
But I know a better spot at night.

47:52.786 --> 47:54.997
-Like where?
-It's a place where no one goes.

47:56.164 --> 47:57.291
And it's nice and quiet.

48:04.172 --> 48:05.048
Hey, don't laugh.

48:05.132 --> 48:05.799
Shush!

48:07.301 --> 48:08.594
Excuse me, hello.

48:09.845 --> 48:11.722
This patient's a friend of mine,
I'll handle it.

48:11.805 --> 48:12.723
Oh, sure.

48:13.265 --> 48:14.850
-Appreciate it.
-Of course, bye.

48:20.981 --> 48:24.192
Just trying to get over here was
extremely treacherous, you know.

48:24.276 --> 48:25.527
So just help me, okay?

48:25.611 --> 48:26.236
Yeah, alright.

48:26.737 --> 48:27.863
I'll take care of it.

48:27.946 --> 48:31.116
But just quit begging, we're friends,
I'm here for you no matter what.

48:31.199 --> 48:33.327
Hey, I told you to stop laughing, already.

48:33.410 --> 48:35.412
This is driving me insane, I swear, jeez.

48:41.293 --> 48:42.544
I mean, how on earth did you manage

48:42.628 --> 48:43.587
to do this to yourself?

48:43.670 --> 48:45.380
I guess there was superglue on the desk,

48:45.464 --> 48:47.716
and I leaned my elbow on the tube,
which caused it to…

48:47.799 --> 48:49.343
drip down from the edges of the desk.

48:49.426 --> 48:50.260
Right.

48:50.802 --> 48:52.512
So then I tried to catch all
the drips with my hand, and,

48:52.596 --> 48:53.513
this is the end result.

48:53.597 --> 48:55.682
You're out of work if you
screw up your hands.

48:55.766 --> 48:58.477
-Just an unemployed loser.
-Yeah, I know all that, Jung-man,

48:58.560 --> 49:00.312
alright? That's why I'm begging you.

49:00.395 --> 49:03.273
Amen, namaste, sawadee kap, I need you.

49:04.107 --> 49:04.942
Mm?

49:05.525 --> 49:06.360
Oh,

49:06.985 --> 49:08.028
on my side, here.

49:08.111 --> 49:09.112
Ugh, God.

49:14.117 --> 49:15.077
Ah, I can't get it, help me,

49:15.160 --> 49:16.078
hold it.

49:17.746 --> 49:18.664
Face recognition worked.

49:22.793 --> 49:23.543
Ugh, God!

49:24.044 --> 49:25.045
Ugh, the things you-

49:25.629 --> 49:27.255
Oh, God. Ugh, typo, typo.

49:31.051 --> 49:32.052
Yes, I did it! It's done!

49:32.552 --> 49:34.096
-Jeez.
-Now slide it on in.

49:38.475 --> 49:39.393
Let's look.

49:39.476 --> 49:42.521
Hey, is an obstetrician
really the right person to do this?

49:42.604 --> 49:43.271
Yes.

49:44.272 --> 49:45.273
Oh my gosh, hold on.

49:45.857 --> 49:47.192
There's a specialist for this.

49:47.275 --> 49:48.485
She's in the hospital now.

49:48.568 --> 49:49.569
Where? Derm, or what?

49:49.653 --> 49:50.654
OR? Or,

49:50.737 --> 49:51.446
It's not Psych?

49:51.947 --> 49:52.447
Not them, no.

49:52.948 --> 49:54.157
Can't you just help me out yourself?
Professor,

49:54.241 --> 49:55.617
you can take the lead surgeon role,

49:55.701 --> 49:57.202
and then I can be the best assistant.

49:57.285 --> 49:59.871
How did you even think to come to
our hospital instead of your own?

49:59.955 --> 50:00.872
You're such a nuisance.

50:00.956 --> 50:03.417
-This place is closer to where I live.
-And not that you were too

50:03.500 --> 50:04.918
embarrassed to get seen at your own.

50:06.753 --> 50:07.337
Oh,

50:07.838 --> 50:08.797
she's here.

50:08.880 --> 50:10.590
-The specialist.
-Well, who is it, then?

50:10.674 --> 50:11.383
Or have we met?

50:12.467 --> 50:15.554
No one comes even close to being her
match, she's a master physician.

50:15.637 --> 50:16.430
Lee Ik-jun?

50:18.682 --> 50:21.893
Weren't we going to meet at the
campground? What brings you here?

50:24.229 --> 50:25.522
Your hands, what happened?

50:26.440 --> 50:27.524
Now what have you done?

50:31.111 --> 50:32.029
My hands got stuck,

50:33.864 --> 50:34.906
super glue…

50:34.990 --> 50:36.283
Super glue? How'd you do that?

50:36.867 --> 50:39.036
So you know that one camping
lantern that you really like?

50:39.119 --> 50:40.620
I noticed that the handle fell off,

50:40.704 --> 50:41.788
so I tried to fix it.

50:41.872 --> 50:42.706
Ugh, you! Seriously?

50:43.206 --> 50:45.375
I told you to just leave it alone,
didn't I? God.

50:45.459 --> 50:46.251
-Ow.
-Let's see.

50:46.835 --> 50:48.587
-I bet- I bet you're in pain.
-Yeah.

50:48.670 --> 50:50.797
God, what are we going to do with you now?
Ugh, goodness sake.

50:50.881 --> 50:52.466
Song-hwa, what are you doing here, anyway?

50:52.549 --> 50:54.634
Well, I had a paper to revise today,
didn't I tell you that?

50:54.718 --> 50:57.554
Chi-hong was taking awhile with the data,
so I thought I should lend a hand.

50:57.637 --> 50:59.431
So how did you know Song-hwa
was here today?

50:59.514 --> 51:02.601
Song-hwa told me she was on her way over,
so we just grabbed some lunch together,

51:02.684 --> 51:04.811
then I was going to work when I happened
to get a call about your little situation.

51:04.895 --> 51:05.729
Oh.

51:07.230 --> 51:08.106
Jung-min,

51:08.190 --> 51:09.274
what do we do with this?

51:10.650 --> 51:11.985
-Ah.
-Warm saline is our first step,

51:12.069 --> 51:13.153
before any big guns.

51:13.236 --> 51:14.988
And then, depending on what happens,

51:15.072 --> 51:16.656
-OS can always cut them off.
-Hey!

51:16.740 --> 51:17.532
How could you-

51:18.909 --> 51:20.494
Well, you have my sincere sympathies.

51:21.244 --> 51:22.412
Hey, Ik-jun!

51:22.496 --> 51:23.705
Huh? Oh God, now what?

51:23.789 --> 51:24.790
Ik-jun, you here?

51:26.124 --> 51:27.000
Are you okay?

51:28.126 --> 51:29.711
What happened to you? Huh?

51:30.504 --> 51:32.339
Seo Jung-min said you were in the ER.

51:32.881 --> 51:34.341
I was so worried about you.

51:36.885 --> 51:40.430
Well, I just happened to get the phone
call when she was right there, so-

51:40.514 --> 51:41.556
Hi, Ggong.

51:45.393 --> 51:46.478
So how are you these days,

51:47.062 --> 51:47.896
Junie

51:48.438 --> 51:49.439
Oh, uh, good. Mm-hm.

51:51.858 --> 51:52.943
Are you okay?

51:53.026 --> 51:54.069
What did you do to yourself?

51:54.152 --> 51:55.278
You see, um-

51:56.113 --> 51:57.030
Hey, you.

51:57.531 --> 51:59.825
Can't you see that someone else is here,
too?

51:59.908 --> 52:00.867
Oh my gosh, Song-hwa!

52:01.451 --> 52:02.786
Oh, it's been so long, wow!

52:03.286 --> 52:04.704
Well, how are you doing?

52:06.289 --> 52:08.500
-You've gotten even prettier now.
-That's not true.

52:09.000 --> 52:10.544
I know, right? Song-hwa gets,

52:10.627 --> 52:12.337
prettier by the day, it's amazing.

52:12.921 --> 52:14.256
Gi-sun, it really has been forever, huh?

52:14.339 --> 52:17.592
You're still the same as you were
three years ago, oh my goodness!

52:17.676 --> 52:20.345
Yes, she hasn't changed at all,
in either looks or skills.

52:20.428 --> 52:21.346
Ugh, here, look.

52:22.889 --> 52:25.934
Song-hwa, look at this. Ugh,
it hurts, it's starting to really sting,

52:26.017 --> 52:26.726
you know?

52:26.810 --> 52:28.854
-Does it sting a lot?
-Yeah, it really hurts! Oh, your hair-

52:28.937 --> 52:29.980
Here, just let me-

52:30.564 --> 52:31.439
Ugh, just quit it!

52:31.523 --> 52:34.401
You need to start focusing on yourself
right now, look at the state you're in!

52:34.484 --> 52:35.944
What do we do about this, ugh.

52:36.027 --> 52:37.654
Hey, don't try to force your hands apart1

52:37.737 --> 52:38.947
No, I won't, but still,
it really does sting, now.

52:39.030 --> 52:39.823
What's going on?

52:40.323 --> 52:41.366
What do you mean?

52:42.159 --> 52:43.618
Your first love is
happily here with his last love.

52:43.702 --> 52:44.995
Hey, stop goofing around.

52:45.078 --> 52:46.538
-They've dated a while now.
-See? They're really stuck.

52:46.621 --> 52:48.123
-Didn't you know?
-I said stop goofing around,

52:48.206 --> 52:49.124
you'll hurt yourself, come on!

52:49.207 --> 52:50.584
Oh, so that's why you-

52:50.667 --> 52:52.961
I'm not goofing around, I'm just
trying to get my hands unstuck!

52:53.044 --> 52:54.087
Hey I already knew they were dating.

52:54.171 --> 52:55.297
Look here. You're banned from camping for

52:55.380 --> 52:56.256
the time being, understand?

52:56.339 --> 52:58.550
-Now how about here? Here?
-Yeah, ow! It hurts!

52:58.633 --> 52:59.509
-Now the other one is starting to hurt!
-You should get the

52:59.593 --> 53:00.468
-lipstick off your teeth.
-Alright, don't look at it.

53:00.552 --> 53:01.344
-Stop looking, stop looking.
-I- Oh, this isn't going to work.

53:01.428 --> 53:02.053
No it's not.

53:02.554 --> 53:03.597
Cham Cham Cham.

53:03.680 --> 53:04.973
Ugh, God! Oh.

53:05.932 --> 53:07.225
Kay, Cham Cham Cham.

53:07.976 --> 53:08.560
I,

53:09.060 --> 53:09.728
I won that round.

53:10.228 --> 53:10.937
-I did.
-Ow. Hey,

53:11.438 --> 53:12.439
stop cheating! You can't
just hit me like that, I-

53:12.522 --> 53:14.065
How is that cheat- Oh,
oh my gosh, right, oh no.

53:14.149 --> 53:15.650
You see how I'm treated here? Gosh.

53:16.151 --> 53:18.069
-Did I hurt you? Are you okay?
-No, it's okay.

53:18.153 --> 53:21.239
-Why won't anyone get me unstuck?
-I'm sorry, I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

53:21.323 --> 53:22.199
Ugh, God.

53:22.282 --> 53:23.408
Seriously?

53:25.243 --> 53:28.872
If the surgery in the OR is running long
and looks like it's going to delay

53:28.955 --> 53:29.915
my surgery,

53:29.998 --> 53:32.667
why can't you take more initiative
and get another OR ready?

53:33.168 --> 53:35.086
If you're incapable of booking an OR,

53:35.170 --> 53:38.548
then I don't understand why you're
here and why we pay you for it.

53:39.216 --> 53:40.091
What is it?

53:40.175 --> 53:42.802
Is it that you don't have any interest
in these surgeries since they're not

53:42.886 --> 53:44.804
-from Obstetrics?
-Hold on just a second.

53:44.888 --> 53:45.597
Or is it,

53:46.181 --> 53:48.225
that you only care if it's
a rare obstetric case?

53:48.308 --> 53:51.895
Hey, you didn't join OBGYN, did you?
You must have only joined OB, huh?

53:51.978 --> 53:52.979
Professor!

54:00.362 --> 54:01.529
Please stick to the issue,

54:02.030 --> 54:05.200
that you were upset with her about
concerning the OR. It seems like,

54:05.283 --> 54:06.826
the rest may be unrelated to it,

54:06.910 --> 54:08.912
and so piling all of it on isn't helpful,
now.

54:09.412 --> 54:10.538
I-

54:11.498 --> 54:13.041
Professor, sorry, but-
just who are you talking to-

54:13.124 --> 54:14.376
Professor!

54:17.963 --> 54:19.339
You know I'm talking to you.

54:20.257 --> 54:21.549
Let's not play games, please.

54:24.302 --> 54:25.720
If someone has made an error,

54:26.680 --> 54:27.764
they should be corrected.

54:27.847 --> 54:28.848
However,

54:30.892 --> 54:33.019
our line of work dictates common courtesy.

54:34.521 --> 54:35.772
You should watch what yo say.

54:43.488 --> 54:44.531
Professor,

54:44.614 --> 54:45.699
the one who needs some,

54:46.199 --> 54:48.118
courtesy right now appears to be you.

54:59.087 --> 54:59.963
You think,

55:00.463 --> 55:01.631
I do this just for fun?

55:01.715 --> 55:02.632
Huh?

55:03.133 --> 55:05.176
This is how you instruct and
guide residents, you buffoon.

55:05.260 --> 55:07.721
Oh, name calling? And I'm
acting like a buffoon right now?

55:08.221 --> 55:09.264
Listen here.

55:10.724 --> 55:13.393
How dare you scream at a resident
in public like that.

55:13.935 --> 55:16.146
How dare you question her
as if she had malintent?

55:16.646 --> 55:19.524
Is neither discipline nor guidance
as far as I'm concerned!

55:22.944 --> 55:24.237
And I'm absolutely sure,

55:25.113 --> 55:27.949
Doctor Kim has fully understood
what it is she did wrong.

55:28.533 --> 55:29.659
Isn't that right, Doctor?

55:33.496 --> 55:34.873
So professor, that's enough.

55:43.089 --> 55:43.965
Of course.

55:44.049 --> 55:45.425
Mm. I was,

55:46.134 --> 55:47.135
about to say the same thing.

55:47.218 --> 55:50.638
Anyway, there's need for anger,
let's keep things pleasant here, huh?

55:51.681 --> 55:53.850
Alright,
then, I apologize. Yes, I'm sorry.

55:54.351 --> 55:56.394
Get back to work,
then, nothing more to see here,

55:56.478 --> 55:57.437
alright? Yes? Good.

56:09.532 --> 56:10.950
Doctor Kim, I'm sorry.

56:12.869 --> 56:13.953
I couldn't hear.

56:14.829 --> 56:16.289
Did you get an apology or not?

56:19.250 --> 56:21.002
Sorry, give me just a second, then.

56:22.587 --> 56:23.463
Professor.

56:26.758 --> 56:27.675
He did apologize.

56:28.968 --> 56:29.844
I heard it,

56:29.928 --> 56:31.137
I did get an apology.

56:31.221 --> 56:32.514
Thanks for your help.

56:36.184 --> 56:37.185
Well, if you say so.

56:50.365 --> 56:51.783
Ugh, that guy,
how could he speak to his senior

56:51.866 --> 56:53.284
like that? In front of the kids, no less.

56:53.368 --> 56:54.828
Ow! Hey, watch where you're-

56:59.707 --> 57:00.500
Uh, I do apologize.

57:00.583 --> 57:02.836
But you're not hurt,
I trust, are you? I work here as, uh,

57:02.919 --> 57:04.212
one of the professors.

57:04.295 --> 57:05.380
Yeah, so?

57:06.589 --> 57:08.591
There are sick people here,
Professor, huh?

57:08.675 --> 57:09.843
You should be careful, then.

57:10.427 --> 57:11.261
Yes.

57:11.761 --> 57:12.679
And I apologize.

57:25.191 --> 57:25.775
Oh, I- I didn't,

57:26.359 --> 57:27.485
s-s-swear at all, not once.

57:27.569 --> 57:28.403
Ah.

57:31.364 --> 57:31.990
I don't raise my-

57:32.490 --> 57:33.783
my voice with anyone either,
just so you know.

57:33.867 --> 57:35.994
Mm, and I speak to people
very courteously now.

57:36.077 --> 57:38.371
Ah! That's so good to hear,
that's good to hear.

57:38.455 --> 57:39.330
You know,

57:39.414 --> 57:41.916
it's wonderful to see you with such
a big smile on your face, too.

57:42.000 --> 57:44.419
And when you smile,
I can see that you're actually,

57:44.502 --> 57:46.671
-just a teddy bear kind of guy, right?
-You think?

57:47.714 --> 57:49.132
Oh, uh, sorry, were you in a hurry, or-?

57:49.215 --> 57:50.341
Just making the rounds.

57:50.967 --> 57:52.844
Your mom's recovery is going really well,
I can say.

57:52.927 --> 57:54.304
Her labs are looking really good.

57:55.305 --> 57:56.139
You really helped so much.

57:56.222 --> 57:57.015
Oh, no, it wasn't me!

57:57.599 --> 58:00.560
Your smile is actually the real
source of her recovery, I think.

58:00.643 --> 58:01.519
Always a pleasure.

58:02.687 --> 58:03.605
I really hope that,

58:04.230 --> 58:05.148
you'll go on,

58:05.231 --> 58:05.940
smiling,

58:06.024 --> 58:06.483
-I will.
-okay?

58:06.983 --> 58:07.650
Well,

58:07.734 --> 58:08.860
-goodbye.
-Great, see you.

58:08.943 --> 58:10.737
JONGNO YULJE MEDICAL CENTER

58:21.915 --> 58:23.416
OH JOO-YOUNG

58:30.340 --> 58:31.174
Pyo Nam-kyung.

58:32.467 --> 58:33.092
Yes?

58:33.676 --> 58:34.511
And Oh Yi-young.

58:35.678 --> 58:37.764
Are you guys in some competition
to be the worst?

58:37.847 --> 58:40.934
Neither of you has kept up with
the charting. And Oh Yi-young,

58:41.017 --> 58:43.269
you haven't done the birth certificates
or delivery records,

58:43.353 --> 58:44.646
Or any patients' discharge work.

58:45.146 --> 58:46.314
You need to get that done.

58:47.357 --> 58:48.942
Pyo Nam-kyung,

58:49.025 --> 58:51.027
you haven't written the admission notes
for any of the surgeries next week.

58:51.110 --> 58:52.362
You need to know all of their details.

58:52.445 --> 58:54.614
-Understand?
-I understand, I'm really sorry.

58:54.697 --> 58:56.074
I'm going into surgery now,

58:56.157 --> 58:58.868
so get those tasks done and show
me before you leave tonight.

58:58.952 --> 58:59.869
Understood?

58:59.953 --> 59:02.288
And I'll check every last detail,
so don't cut corners.

59:02.789 --> 59:03.998
-Will do.
-Will do.

59:16.135 --> 59:16.970
Hello?

59:19.222 --> 59:19.847
Sorry?

59:20.682 --> 59:21.307
Oh,

59:21.891 --> 59:22.850
yes, yes,
I'll go tell the professor immediately.

59:22.934 --> 59:23.851
Alright.

59:30.400 --> 59:31.359
Hello, ma'am?

59:31.442 --> 59:32.527
Ma'am, can you hear me?

59:32.610 --> 59:33.236
Ma'am?

59:33.736 --> 59:34.946
Her hemoglobin count is six point six.

59:35.029 --> 59:36.406
And her BP is falling.

59:36.489 --> 59:37.448
Pump more blood.

59:37.532 --> 59:38.157
Got it.

59:38.658 --> 59:39.701
Ma'am, wake up.

59:39.784 --> 59:41.286
Can you open your eyes for me?

59:41.369 --> 59:42.495
Ma'am, can you tell me your name?

59:42.579 --> 59:43.454
Hello, ma'am?

59:43.538 --> 59:49.043
Yulje EMS, Hotel Lima nine six nine seven,
six mile final, Yulje helipad.

59:55.883 --> 59:56.759
We're here, ma'am.

59:58.219 --> 59:59.429
-We're gonna move you.
-Please lift the stretcher.

59:59.512 --> 01:00:01.264
-One, two, three.
-One, two, three.

01:00:02.348 --> 01:00:04.100
-One, two, three.
-One, two, three.

01:00:05.768 --> 01:00:07.979
She had a precipitous labor
and gave birth two hours ago.

01:00:08.062 --> 01:00:09.606
PPH developed,
a balloon tamponade was placed

01:00:09.689 --> 01:00:10.857
but the bleeding isn't slowing.

01:00:10.940 --> 01:00:13.860
Her BP dropped to seventy over forty
earlier, it's ninety over sixty by our

01:00:13.943 --> 01:00:14.861
last measure.

01:00:14.944 --> 01:00:17.655
She's had a unit of O-negative, and has
a history of DDLT dating back seven years

01:00:17.739 --> 01:00:18.573
ago.

01:00:19.198 --> 01:00:19.824
Oh ma'am, hey!

01:00:20.325 --> 01:00:21.242
Try to open your eyes for me if you can!

01:00:21.326 --> 01:00:22.368
-Ma'am, come on!
-Let's head to the ER to get IV

01:00:22.452 --> 01:00:23.620
access established on the patient.

01:00:23.703 --> 01:00:25.913
Then she'll be transferred
right into the OR.

01:00:28.374 --> 01:00:30.335
Let's get her on a monitor and
assess her vitals right away.

01:00:30.418 --> 01:00:31.127
Yes.

01:00:31.628 --> 01:00:33.588
-And grab the ultrasound for us.
-Will do.

01:00:36.924 --> 01:00:38.718
-Place a central line, now.
-Yes.

01:00:44.349 --> 01:00:45.266
Pyo Nam-kyung.

01:00:47.310 --> 01:00:48.144
Pyo Nam-kyung.

01:00:49.437 --> 01:00:50.396
Hey, Pyo Nam-kyung!

01:00:50.480 --> 01:00:51.439
Oh, oh.

01:00:52.649 --> 01:00:53.566
Yi-young.

01:00:54.192 --> 01:00:55.735
Right, we need to do something fast.

01:00:55.818 --> 01:00:57.403
Mm, oh, I don't think I can.

01:00:58.154 --> 01:00:59.113
No, I can't…

01:00:59.197 --> 01:01:00.615
But we can't just stand here!

01:01:01.532 --> 01:01:02.617
She's bleeding out.

01:01:04.452 --> 01:01:05.536
-Hey!
-Huh?

01:01:06.037 --> 01:01:06.788
She's bleeding out.

01:01:07.288 --> 01:01:08.247
Yeah.

01:01:09.082 --> 01:01:09.957
Bleeding means we-

01:01:10.041 --> 01:01:12.043
That's right,
bleeding, as soon as we notice it-

01:01:12.126 --> 01:01:13.670
the next step is to quickly-

01:01:13.753 --> 01:01:15.630
-Yes, just place the line.
-All right.

01:01:16.297 --> 01:01:17.965
I started the Emergency Protocol…

01:01:18.966 --> 01:01:19.717
Uh-

01:01:21.886 --> 01:01:23.805
Oh, Nurse! Place a Foley catheter.

01:01:24.305 --> 01:01:26.474
And next up is- uh-

01:01:27.642 --> 01:01:28.476
Oh,

01:01:28.976 --> 01:01:31.229
the oxytocin infusion, mix that now,
and carbetocin, do an IV push.

01:01:31.312 --> 01:01:32.021
Okay.

01:01:32.605 --> 01:01:34.691
-Are the labs being sent?
-They are right now, yes.

01:01:38.528 --> 01:01:39.404
Doctor,

01:01:39.987 --> 01:01:41.114
the rapid infusion system,
can you start it?

01:01:41.197 --> 01:01:42.031
Yeah.

01:01:42.865 --> 01:01:43.825
Please open the IV all the way.

01:01:43.908 --> 01:01:44.867
Yes, doing it right now.

01:01:45.368 --> 01:01:47.704
-Alright, it's open.
-Pyo Nam-kyung.

01:01:50.498 --> 01:01:51.958
Hey, get it together!

01:01:54.794 --> 01:01:56.462
Can't you tell I'm scared too?

01:01:59.132 --> 01:01:59.757
Huh?

01:02:00.258 --> 01:02:01.300
Oh, yeah.

01:02:02.677 --> 01:02:03.970
The balloon comes out first, okay?

01:02:06.347 --> 01:02:07.223
Alright.

01:02:16.315 --> 01:02:17.775
-OR, please
-Oh,

01:02:17.859 --> 01:02:18.526
right.

01:02:25.867 --> 01:02:26.868
This is Obstetrics, yeah.

01:02:26.951 --> 01:02:28.119
Is there a prepped OR ready?

01:02:28.619 --> 01:02:30.788
Ugh, please, it's an emergency, hurry up!

01:02:32.707 --> 01:02:33.708
-Oh, Nurse,
-Yes?

01:02:33.791 --> 01:02:35.126
I've contacted the blood bank already.

01:02:35.209 --> 01:02:37.670
In the meantime,
send two units of Universal O to the OR.

01:02:37.754 --> 01:02:39.589
-We're going to need more there.
-Yes.

01:02:39.672 --> 01:02:40.506
-Be quick!
-Okay.

01:02:42.008 --> 01:02:43.634
Doctor, can you place an A-line as well?

01:02:43.718 --> 01:02:44.719
Alright.

01:02:56.647 --> 01:02:57.523
Doctor.

01:02:57.607 --> 01:02:58.524
-Yes?
-The patient's marked

01:02:58.608 --> 01:02:59.650
down as having a DDLT.

01:02:59.734 --> 01:03:00.318
What?

01:03:00.818 --> 01:03:01.402
Oh my God, right.

01:03:01.903 --> 01:03:03.362
The Transplant team has to
check lab results first,

01:03:03.446 --> 01:03:05.406
to clear the patient to
go into surgery and,

01:03:05.490 --> 01:03:06.824
they're not here right now.

01:03:08.534 --> 01:03:09.368
May I?

01:03:09.869 --> 01:03:11.662
Let me see that. Right.

01:03:13.456 --> 01:03:14.957
I work at Yulje Main,
I do Hepatobiliary there.

01:03:15.041 --> 01:03:16.417
-Oh.
-If I could? Thanks.

01:03:17.001 --> 01:03:18.419
Alright then,
how long ago did she get her

01:03:18.503 --> 01:03:19.504
liver transplant, d'you know?

01:03:19.587 --> 01:03:21.088
Oh, she had it seven years ago.

01:03:21.172 --> 01:03:23.257
And then two years ago,
she also gave birth.

01:03:23.758 --> 01:03:25.843
Ah, yeah, her levels all look really good.

01:03:25.927 --> 01:03:28.137
Use antibiotics just like you normally
would. I think it's time,

01:03:28.221 --> 01:03:29.555
for surgery to proceed, now.

01:03:29.639 --> 01:03:31.224
-Alright.
-Oh, there a chance of adhesion,

01:03:31.307 --> 01:03:32.600
so just try to be careful of that.

01:03:32.683 --> 01:03:33.601
Okay, come on.

01:03:33.684 --> 01:03:34.727
-Oh.
-Thanks so much.

01:03:34.811 --> 01:03:35.561
Yeah, thank you.

01:03:36.062 --> 01:03:37.355
Raising the side rails.

01:03:41.150 --> 01:03:43.611
We're moving out now,
please clear the way for us!

01:03:50.284 --> 01:03:51.327
Oh, ma'am!

01:03:51.410 --> 01:03:52.662
Try to stay with us!

01:03:52.745 --> 01:03:53.454
Stay awake, please!

01:03:54.121 --> 01:03:55.623
-I just feel so tired.
-Stay awake!

01:03:55.706 --> 01:03:56.999
Just keep your eyes open

01:03:58.292 --> 01:03:59.252
No, ma'am, don't!

01:03:59.335 --> 01:04:00.127
Please, ma'am!

01:04:01.128 --> 01:04:02.421
You had your second child today!

01:04:03.422 --> 01:04:05.508
It's your baby's birthday,
she's waiting for you.

01:04:05.591 --> 01:04:07.134
You need to take care of her!

01:04:07.218 --> 01:04:08.135
Yes.

01:04:18.646 --> 01:04:19.522
Anesthesia.

01:04:19.605 --> 01:04:20.523
Yes, starting now.

01:04:26.487 --> 01:04:27.572
The patient's multiparous, right?

01:04:27.655 --> 01:04:28.865
Yes, that's right, she is.

01:04:28.948 --> 01:04:30.533
She gave birth two and a half hours ago,

01:04:30.616 --> 01:04:31.701
and the baby is doing okay.

01:04:31.784 --> 01:04:32.660
How much blood loss?

01:04:32.743 --> 01:04:35.329
I'd say she's lost about two
thousand CC's so far, Doctor.

01:04:35.413 --> 01:04:38.791
When we checked with a speculum in the ER,
we noticed active bleeding.

01:04:38.875 --> 01:04:40.167
How much blood has she received?

01:04:40.251 --> 01:04:42.044
She's gotten one unit
already on the chopper,

01:04:42.128 --> 01:04:43.880
and she's on her third unit in total.

01:04:43.963 --> 01:04:45.798
Two units of universal O
were prepped in advance,

01:04:45.882 --> 01:04:49.594
and the blood bank has prepared ten units
of R-B-Cs and five units of F-F-P as well.

01:04:49.677 --> 01:04:50.761
When will they be ready?

01:04:51.262 --> 01:04:52.763
They need around twenty minutes.

01:04:53.264 --> 01:04:55.892
And have the CBC and DIC
lab results come back yet?

01:04:55.975 --> 01:04:56.601
Yes,

01:04:57.101 --> 01:04:58.185
the labs sent from the ER,

01:04:58.269 --> 01:04:59.353
show a CBC of six point two and,

01:04:59.437 --> 01:05:01.105
a platelet count of ninety thousand.

01:05:01.188 --> 01:05:02.523
AST and ALT are both normal,

01:05:02.607 --> 01:05:04.066
but PT and APTT,

01:05:04.609 --> 01:05:05.526
they seem to be

01:05:05.610 --> 01:05:06.569
prolonged, Professor.

01:05:07.069 --> 01:05:07.612
Oh,

01:05:08.112 --> 01:05:09.071
and all other DIC labs,

01:05:09.155 --> 01:05:10.114
are still in progress.

01:05:10.197 --> 01:05:11.824
Good work, that's very well done.

01:05:12.533 --> 01:05:14.076
Pyo Nam-kyung, you go scrub up first.

01:05:16.495 --> 01:05:17.538
I can't do it.

01:05:18.372 --> 01:05:19.415
Then you, Yi-young.

01:05:21.834 --> 01:05:23.878
You two are assisting, get it together!

01:05:24.462 --> 01:05:26.213
-The patient is-
-You guys can leave.

01:05:26.714 --> 01:05:27.715
Wait, your surgery-

01:05:27.798 --> 01:05:28.716
It's all done.

01:05:28.799 --> 01:05:29.967
Professor,

01:05:30.051 --> 01:05:32.470
-the patient, she's really-
-Yes, I'm aware.

01:05:32.553 --> 01:05:33.971
I'm looking at her right now.

01:05:41.020 --> 01:05:41.854
Hey,

01:05:42.563 --> 01:05:43.648
we have no assistants here.

01:05:43.731 --> 01:05:44.732
Yeah, seems to be the case.

01:05:44.815 --> 01:05:47.443
I guess you're the only one
we can rely on right now.

01:05:48.694 --> 01:05:49.528
The BP is dropping.

01:05:50.029 --> 01:05:51.155
It's seventy over forty, now.

01:05:51.238 --> 01:05:52.448
I'll keep up with the fluid volume.

01:05:52.531 --> 01:05:54.450
Don't worry, start the surgery now.

01:05:56.243 --> 01:05:57.286
Alright, then,

01:05:57.787 --> 01:05:58.704
guess we should begin.

01:06:12.635 --> 01:06:15.513
ANESTHESIA ELAPSED TIME
CURRENT TIME, SURGERY ELAPSED TIME

01:06:18.808 --> 01:06:20.184
Kelly scissors.

01:06:23.646 --> 01:06:25.690
-I need another pair.
-Right here.

01:06:27.191 --> 01:06:28.067
Metzenbaum.

01:06:29.318 --> 01:06:30.736
And then prep a one-zero tie.

01:06:37.576 --> 01:06:38.244
Tie.

01:06:44.959 --> 01:06:45.793
Cut.

01:06:50.339 --> 01:06:51.799
Administer the tranexamic acid, please.

01:06:51.882 --> 01:06:52.800
Yes, I'm on it.

01:07:05.104 --> 01:07:05.980
Tonsil.

01:07:09.817 --> 01:07:10.693
Right angle.

01:07:16.907 --> 01:07:17.533
Hold the suction.

01:07:18.034 --> 01:07:18.951
-Yes, Doctor.
-Alright.

01:07:43.517 --> 01:07:45.978
I was worried the adhesion would be
bad due to the liver transplant,

01:07:46.062 --> 01:07:47.605
but the surgery's gone smoothly.

01:07:47.688 --> 01:07:48.564
Yes, it has.

01:07:48.647 --> 01:07:49.690
What a relief.

01:07:52.943 --> 01:07:54.111
So what do you think?

01:07:55.863 --> 01:07:57.114
There's no bleeding.

01:07:57.698 --> 01:07:58.115
What else?

01:07:59.992 --> 01:08:00.910
The patient,

01:08:03.746 --> 01:08:04.663
has been saved.

01:08:05.164 --> 01:08:06.165
And now…

01:08:07.792 --> 01:08:09.126
she can meet her baby.

01:08:10.628 --> 01:08:11.754
Not that sort of stuff!

01:08:12.338 --> 01:08:14.215
She's lost four thousand CC of blood,

01:08:14.298 --> 01:08:16.842
but her vitals are still
holding stable right now.

01:08:16.926 --> 01:08:17.510
Yes

01:08:18.010 --> 01:08:18.761
Her vitals…

01:08:19.261 --> 01:08:20.304
are all normal, Doctor.

01:08:20.387 --> 01:08:21.263
If you ask me,

01:08:21.806 --> 01:08:23.140
the surgery went very well.

01:08:47.998 --> 01:08:49.500
-Hey.
-What?

01:08:50.042 --> 01:08:51.669
Go write the surgical record already.

01:08:51.752 --> 01:08:53.963
Why would I do all that
when we have the residents?

01:08:54.046 --> 01:08:56.215
You really think they'll
recall anything at all?

01:08:56.298 --> 01:08:57.424
Thanks to the two of us,

01:08:57.508 --> 01:08:58.884
they came down off the cliff.

01:08:58.968 --> 01:09:02.263
Ugh, you're supposed to write it 'cause
you stepped in first to lead the surgery.

01:09:02.346 --> 01:09:04.056
It's always the assistant that writes it!

01:09:04.557 --> 01:09:05.850
You came in to assist, right?

01:09:06.684 --> 01:09:09.436
I was in too much shock to really
pay any attention okay?

01:09:09.520 --> 01:09:10.437
Hey,

01:09:11.021 --> 01:09:13.357
you've been doing this
too long to get shocked.

01:09:13.440 --> 01:09:16.068
-You always deal with hemorrhages.
-You're one to talk.

01:09:16.152 --> 01:09:17.194
Hey,

01:09:17.278 --> 01:09:19.155
I saw your hands tremble
earlier and I thought,

01:09:19.238 --> 01:09:20.072
Ah,

01:09:21.198 --> 01:09:23.576
so this is what it means
to 'shake like a leaf'.

01:09:24.785 --> 01:09:27.121
If I were shaking,
I wouldn't have done a perfect surgery.

01:09:27.204 --> 01:09:29.039
Please, perfect according to who? Ugh.

01:09:29.123 --> 01:09:30.166
Now, girls,

01:09:31.458 --> 01:09:32.626
let's be pleasant, huh?

01:09:33.419 --> 01:09:34.086
Hm?

01:09:34.587 --> 01:09:35.796
Try something. Please say:

01:09:35.880 --> 01:09:37.173
"Hey, I wanted to say thanks."

01:09:37.256 --> 01:09:39.091
Aw, good job. "Wow, great work." But no,

01:09:39.592 --> 01:09:42.136
you're just at each other's
throats like you've been,

01:09:42.219 --> 01:09:44.054
for twenty years now. Ugh, goodness.

01:09:44.138 --> 01:09:45.514
Ugh, ugh, it's just too sad.

01:09:46.348 --> 01:09:47.766
Ugh, I can't take it, you two.

01:09:48.851 --> 01:09:49.685
Gosh.

01:09:51.061 --> 01:09:51.979
Ugh, Gosh.

01:09:56.859 --> 01:09:58.986
Great work,
thanks, good job. There, how's that?

01:09:59.486 --> 01:10:00.654
Whatever.

01:10:00.738 --> 01:10:02.698
Ugh, I'm so sick of this.

01:10:04.241 --> 01:10:05.367
Gosh, those two.

01:10:05.951 --> 01:10:06.869
Professor.

01:10:07.953 --> 01:10:09.496
Oh dear, the surgery's finished.

01:10:09.580 --> 01:10:10.414
Sorry?

01:10:10.915 --> 01:10:12.208
The Obstetrics emergency surgery.

01:10:12.708 --> 01:10:13.459
Oh,

01:10:13.959 --> 01:10:15.628
-apparently, it went well.
-Ah.

01:10:20.007 --> 01:10:20.883
Where are you going?

01:10:20.966 --> 01:10:21.717
Aren't you done?

01:10:24.053 --> 01:10:24.720
I was,

01:10:25.221 --> 01:10:26.513
going to assist your surgery.

01:10:27.014 --> 01:10:28.515
It's a laparoscopy,
so someone has to hold

01:10:28.599 --> 01:10:29.516
the uterine manipulator.

01:10:30.226 --> 01:10:30.935
Uh,

01:10:31.435 --> 01:10:33.520
I was going to head into surgery first
to put it in place because the fellow

01:10:33.604 --> 01:10:34.897
said they were going to be late.

01:10:35.397 --> 01:10:36.774
I thought I would do it.

01:10:36.857 --> 01:10:38.776
And I've already let the other guy know.

01:10:40.444 --> 01:10:42.321
Uh- No, it's okay.

01:10:42.404 --> 01:10:43.447
You can go home.

01:10:43.530 --> 01:10:44.865
You've had a long day, huh?

01:10:45.991 --> 01:10:46.617
Uh…

01:10:47.117 --> 01:10:48.035
It's all right, go.

01:10:48.535 --> 01:10:50.621
It's fine,
I can manage perfectly well by myself.

01:10:51.580 --> 01:10:52.414
Oh.

01:10:55.751 --> 01:10:57.878
Look,
I'm really fine, don't worry about it.

01:11:00.839 --> 01:11:02.174
I'm fine too, and I'd like,

01:11:02.258 --> 01:11:03.801
to observe your surgery.

01:11:06.053 --> 01:11:07.596
Oh, oh, are you serious?

01:11:07.680 --> 01:11:08.555
So you mean it?

01:11:08.639 --> 01:11:10.849
Then would you like to take an RSO,
do you think?

01:11:10.933 --> 01:11:11.892
I'd love that!

01:11:11.976 --> 01:11:13.519
-Thanks so much!
-Oh, oh, you would?

01:11:13.602 --> 01:11:14.395
Well, in that case, uh-

01:11:14.895 --> 01:11:15.646
we can-

01:11:16.313 --> 01:11:18.315
Yes, Professor,
the patient's stabilized, now.

01:11:18.816 --> 01:11:20.693
I told the Air Ambulance
team that everything's

01:11:20.776 --> 01:11:22.778
alright and passed on our team's thanks.

01:11:24.530 --> 01:11:25.197
Yes,

01:11:25.698 --> 01:11:27.116
course, I'll check up on her.

01:11:27.908 --> 01:11:28.993
Alright, then.

01:11:37.501 --> 01:11:38.627
What did you put?

01:11:38.711 --> 01:11:40.045
Just the patient info here.

01:11:42.589 --> 01:11:43.340
You guys done?

01:11:44.466 --> 01:11:46.093
Can we have some more time, please?

01:11:46.176 --> 01:11:49.179
It's not that we didn't try,
we just couldn't because there was-

01:11:49.263 --> 01:11:51.098
-Well, there was this-
-Yeah, I know.

01:11:53.350 --> 01:11:55.352
The patient asked me
to send on her thanks.

01:11:55.436 --> 01:11:57.938
She said one of you kept
her awake on the way,

01:11:58.022 --> 01:11:59.773
and one reminded her to go see her child.

01:12:00.274 --> 01:12:01.400
And I bet that's you.

01:12:04.695 --> 01:12:05.487
You guys…

01:12:06.280 --> 01:12:07.531
did really well today.

01:12:08.032 --> 01:12:09.992
I know it must've been
completely terrifying,

01:12:10.075 --> 01:12:11.327
and difficult, and chaotic.

01:12:13.704 --> 01:12:14.955
Now since the two of you…

01:12:15.456 --> 01:12:17.166
did such great work today,

01:12:21.420 --> 01:12:22.463
I'm gonna finish these.

01:12:22.546 --> 01:12:23.380
Sorry?

01:12:28.177 --> 01:12:29.720
-Unless you don't want me to.
-Oh, no!

01:12:29.803 --> 01:12:30.721
That's not the case.

01:12:33.140 --> 01:12:35.517
Get outta here or I'll change my mind,
so go on.

01:12:37.478 --> 01:12:38.604
In three.

01:12:40.230 --> 01:12:41.106
Okay then.

01:12:41.190 --> 01:12:42.066
Thanks a lot, bye!

01:12:42.149 --> 01:12:43.067
Thanks a bunch!

01:12:51.909 --> 01:12:53.535
I'll see you there in two hours.

01:12:56.538 --> 01:12:57.664
Aren't you hungry?

01:12:57.748 --> 01:12:59.208
You haven't eaten all day.

01:12:59.291 --> 01:13:02.044
Don't talk to me.
I can barely walk because I'm so hungry.

01:13:02.127 --> 01:13:02.961
Yeah?

01:13:03.712 --> 01:13:04.588
Want some of this?

01:13:04.671 --> 01:13:05.923
Someone gave me these.

01:13:06.757 --> 01:13:07.383
Here.

01:13:10.677 --> 01:13:11.929
There are only two of them.

01:13:12.513 --> 01:13:14.223
The others'll probably be hungry, too.

01:13:14.723 --> 01:13:15.933
Should you and I just,

01:13:18.060 --> 01:13:19.353
eat it ourselves in secret?

01:13:20.354 --> 01:13:21.021
That seems selfish.

01:13:21.522 --> 01:13:22.815
Shouldn't we wait?

01:13:22.898 --> 01:13:24.483
These are too famous to wait for.

01:13:24.566 --> 01:13:28.278
Because they sell out, you can't get any,
no matter what, without a big line.

01:13:28.362 --> 01:13:29.363
Even so-

01:13:30.239 --> 01:13:31.573
You saw them both arguing, didn't you?

01:13:31.657 --> 01:13:32.491
Mm-hm.

01:13:33.033 --> 01:13:35.619
They need some alone time, then.
They're ashamed to be seen apologizing.

01:13:36.370 --> 01:13:37.037
Oh.

01:13:37.538 --> 01:13:40.541
We need to give them privacy,
it's really all for their own good.

01:13:41.083 --> 01:13:41.625
Is it?

01:13:43.001 --> 01:13:44.169
Then we better,

01:13:45.712 --> 01:13:46.505
just go, huh?

01:13:48.006 --> 01:13:48.841
So where should we eat?

01:13:49.341 --> 01:13:50.259
Ah!

01:13:50.342 --> 01:13:51.718
The place I told you about!

01:13:52.219 --> 01:13:53.470
Ah, that one?

01:13:53.554 --> 01:13:54.471
Mm-hm.

01:13:55.013 --> 01:13:56.682
It's gonna be empty, now. Let's go.

01:14:02.980 --> 01:14:04.690
It's been so long,
I think I might've- ugh.

01:14:04.773 --> 01:14:05.941
Maybe this isn't the right way.

01:14:06.024 --> 01:14:06.942
It's the right way.

01:14:07.609 --> 01:14:09.778
If we go up there and take a left,
and then just keep going,

01:14:09.862 --> 01:14:11.572
there are escalators,
and once we take those down,

01:14:11.655 --> 01:14:12.739
we'll be in the lobby.

01:14:14.658 --> 01:14:17.077
Song-hwa,
your brain's amazing, you know so much.

01:14:18.078 --> 01:14:19.413
There's a sign right there…

01:14:19.496 --> 01:14:20.122
Oh!

01:14:20.622 --> 01:14:21.665
Oh, I guess I missed that.

01:14:22.166 --> 01:14:24.460
I was so captivated by you,
that explains it.

01:14:26.336 --> 01:14:27.588
-Hey, you know,
-Mm?

01:14:27.671 --> 01:14:29.381
Being here at night,
the outpatient clinic

01:14:29.465 --> 01:14:30.507
seems a little scary.

01:14:31.133 --> 01:14:32.050
It's completely deserted.

01:14:32.551 --> 01:14:33.594
No, it isn't.

01:14:34.178 --> 01:14:35.012
There's someone here.

01:14:37.723 --> 01:14:38.724
Who else is here?

01:14:43.604 --> 01:14:45.272
Stop messing with me,
nobody's here, right?

01:14:45.355 --> 01:14:47.316
Hey, seriously, stop with that!

01:14:47.399 --> 01:14:48.567
It isn't anything scary.

01:14:49.359 --> 01:14:50.444
I think there could be,

01:14:50.527 --> 01:14:52.070
bugs scampering around here.

01:14:52.154 --> 01:14:53.280
Bugs? Do you mean that?

01:14:53.780 --> 01:14:55.574
But this is a hospital,
come on, there are no bugs.

01:14:55.657 --> 01:14:57.743
Of course I don't mean real bugs, come on.

01:14:58.452 --> 01:15:00.662
I'm talking about is couples
on secret dates.

01:15:01.663 --> 01:15:03.457
-Hm.
-With nowhere to go,

01:15:03.957 --> 01:15:05.250
and barely and time off,

01:15:05.334 --> 01:15:06.960
they still have to go on dates, you know?

01:15:07.044 --> 01:15:08.545
So they come along, searching,

01:15:08.629 --> 01:15:11.173
for the rare,
empty places the hospitals always have.

01:15:11.256 --> 01:15:12.049
So what?

01:15:12.674 --> 01:15:13.675
Just where do they all go?

01:15:14.176 --> 01:15:15.093
Emergency stairs?

01:15:15.594 --> 01:15:17.262
-On-call area?
-God, no!

01:15:17.763 --> 01:15:19.515
That's only if they want to be found out,
you goof.

01:15:19.598 --> 01:15:20.516
Somewhere-

01:15:21.683 --> 01:15:22.851
Wait, here?

01:15:25.145 --> 01:15:26.438
Exactly, yeah.

01:15:27.105 --> 01:15:29.816
Appointments are all done,
no patients, the staff's gone home…

01:15:29.900 --> 01:15:30.609
Oh.

01:15:31.109 --> 01:15:32.986
They come here, by night,

01:15:33.487 --> 01:15:34.655
to go on their little secret dates.

01:15:34.738 --> 01:15:36.156
Still,
the professors could forget something,

01:15:36.240 --> 01:15:37.366
and return to the clinic to get it.

01:15:37.449 --> 01:15:38.575
Oh my God.

01:15:38.659 --> 01:15:40.827
-They swing the door open, hit the lights.
-Yeah?

01:15:41.411 --> 01:15:42.454
Then something scuttles away,

01:15:42.538 --> 01:15:44.498
-as they all disappear like bugs do.
-So where do they hide?

01:15:44.581 --> 01:15:45.707
Well, uh,

01:15:46.750 --> 01:15:48.669
they back up against the wall,
or hide behind a door, or they might even,

01:15:48.752 --> 01:15:51.713
crawl under the desk to keep hidden
so they don't get caught.

01:15:54.299 --> 01:15:54.800
Okay, but how,

01:15:56.718 --> 01:15:59.054
do you know all those details,
then, exactly?

01:16:01.807 --> 01:16:03.809
Must've had some dates way back then.

01:16:04.851 --> 01:16:05.727
Well, it wasn't-

01:16:06.311 --> 01:16:08.438
Hey, it was all Jun-wan, alright?

01:16:09.273 --> 01:16:10.857
When he was still a resident here, yeah.

01:16:10.941 --> 01:16:12.693
And he would do it all the time,
that's how I know.

01:16:12.776 --> 01:16:13.610
I see.

01:16:16.697 --> 01:16:18.198
Think there are bugs here now?

01:16:18.740 --> 01:16:19.408
Wait,

01:16:19.992 --> 01:16:21.535
hey, what are you doing? Don't!

01:16:23.954 --> 01:16:25.747
This isn't even our hospital, quit it.

01:16:27.374 --> 01:16:28.292
Hear anything?

01:16:29.585 --> 01:16:30.836
I think I hear something.

01:16:32.379 --> 01:16:33.630
What's this? What's this?

01:16:34.423 --> 01:16:37.217
-I thought I heard a knock.
-Oh my God, you're not hearing anything.

01:16:37.301 --> 01:16:39.928
-There's nobody down here, knock it off.
-Oh, Song- Song-hwa, was it you knocking?

01:16:40.012 --> 01:16:40.887
Oh, you scared me!

01:16:41.680 --> 01:16:42.639
Hey, let's go.

01:16:43.181 --> 01:16:44.349
I'll spare them for now.

01:16:45.392 --> 01:16:47.060
Actually, I assume that kids these days,

01:16:47.144 --> 01:16:48.228
don't bother coming here.

01:16:48.729 --> 01:16:50.981
I see them holding hands just out in
the open and getting coffee together

01:16:51.064 --> 01:16:51.815
and things.

01:16:52.316 --> 01:16:54.318
That's just barely scratching the
surface here, don't you see? Gosh.

01:16:54.401 --> 01:16:55.193
Song-hwa,

01:16:55.694 --> 01:16:58.405
there are five hundred and twenty
kids out on secret dates,

01:16:58.488 --> 01:17:00.866
all in places just like this,
right this second.

01:17:01.450 --> 01:17:02.117
Here, see?

01:17:02.701 --> 01:17:05.495
Hang on, stop it.
What if there really is someone there?

01:17:08.832 --> 01:17:10.375
Look at that, you see it now, right?

01:17:10.459 --> 01:17:12.169
Guess those days are all long over.

01:17:12.252 --> 01:17:14.588
These MZers aren't like
that and you know it.

01:17:15.380 --> 01:17:16.590
No, I think you're wrong.

01:17:16.673 --> 01:17:19.217
I was busting plenty of them just last
year, I know they still use it.

01:17:19.301 --> 01:17:20.093
Huh.

01:17:20.927 --> 01:17:23.305
I guess the bugs really
did disappear after all.

01:17:24.097 --> 01:17:25.349
Wanna get something for dinner?

01:17:25.432 --> 01:17:27.267
Oh, the guys want us to go and join
them, we're all celebrating your

01:17:27.351 --> 01:17:28.226
-discharge.
-Mm.

01:17:28.310 --> 01:17:29.353
-They want ramyeon.
-Alright, let's get

01:17:29.436 --> 01:17:30.562
some gimbap on the way-

01:17:32.773 --> 01:17:33.857
Wait, you told them already?

01:17:33.940 --> 01:17:34.608
Look,

01:17:35.108 --> 01:17:36.902
I really didn't mean to tell anyone, okay?

01:17:36.985 --> 01:17:39.237
They just kept asking where we were and
when we were coming, and things sort of

01:17:39.321 --> 01:17:40.364
came out while we were talking, and-

01:17:40.447 --> 01:17:43.200
Ugh, if they know, the entire
hospital knows what an idiot I am.

01:17:43.283 --> 01:17:44.451
-Oh, I'm sorry.
-Ugh…

01:17:45.535 --> 01:17:47.537
I should've gone to our hospital
if everybody was going find out.

01:17:47.621 --> 01:17:50.666
I drove all the way to Jongno,
and now everybody knows about it anyway.

01:17:50.749 --> 01:17:51.583
Ugh.

01:17:52.584 --> 01:17:53.460
I know.

01:17:55.629 --> 01:17:56.338
Hey, are you,

01:17:56.838 --> 01:17:57.798
really okay now, or not?

01:17:58.298 --> 01:17:59.633
Nothing is okay, not at all!

01:18:00.217 --> 01:18:02.469
I was praying for hours and hours
today with my hands stuck together,

01:18:02.552 --> 01:18:04.388
and they nearly combusted, feel this!

01:18:05.472 --> 01:18:08.558
Hey, that really was such a lucky
miss you had today, you know.

01:18:08.642 --> 01:18:10.686
-Ah.
-Could you please be more careful?

01:18:10.769 --> 01:18:13.397
Ugh, I'm never going to hear the
end of this from those guys, am I?

01:18:13.480 --> 01:18:14.398
I can't believe it.

01:18:15.107 --> 01:18:17.943
Hey, is this door supposed to be open?
What do you think?

01:18:18.568 --> 01:18:19.986
Should we close it behind us?

01:18:28.495 --> 01:18:29.830
It's alright, they're gone.

01:18:31.748 --> 01:18:33.291
Ugh, God, those guys scared me.

01:18:34.209 --> 01:18:35.127
Why did we,

01:18:36.002 --> 01:18:37.129
hide in the first place?

01:18:37.212 --> 01:18:38.213
Huh?

01:18:38.839 --> 01:18:39.923
Why tell me to hide down there?

01:18:40.006 --> 01:18:41.675
It's not like we aren't allowed in here.

01:18:42.175 --> 01:18:43.468
Did I tell you to hide?

01:18:43.552 --> 01:18:44.261
No.

01:18:44.761 --> 01:18:47.139
You actually pushed me under
the desk without warning.

01:18:47.222 --> 01:18:49.391
You sat next to me and went, Shh!

01:18:50.100 --> 01:18:50.851
Just like that.

01:18:51.685 --> 01:18:52.310
Did I?

01:18:54.730 --> 01:18:55.814
W- w- why did I do that?

01:18:57.149 --> 01:18:58.400
Well, it's 'cause I was worried-

01:18:58.900 --> 01:18:59.651
Uh-

01:19:00.152 --> 01:19:00.944
Oh,

01:19:01.445 --> 01:19:02.612
I thought we'd get scolded
for not working.

01:19:02.696 --> 01:19:03.280
We're done with work.

01:19:03.780 --> 01:19:04.698
That's right.

01:19:08.660 --> 01:19:09.286
Wow,

01:19:09.786 --> 01:19:10.746
even in that moment,

01:19:10.829 --> 01:19:13.582
you remembered every detail of
what I did just to criticize it.

01:19:13.665 --> 01:19:15.000
Is it because you're smart?

01:19:22.674 --> 01:19:24.426
Hang on. Forgot my coat.

01:19:31.600 --> 01:19:32.434
Here.

01:19:33.101 --> 01:19:34.186
Streusel buns sound good to you?

01:19:34.269 --> 01:19:35.103
Yeah.

01:19:39.024 --> 01:19:40.484
-I'm so hungry.
-Oh, are you?

01:19:40.567 --> 01:19:41.193
Yeah, aren't you?

01:19:41.276 --> 01:19:41.902
Yeah.

01:19:42.402 --> 01:19:43.487
Oh, man, I got you.

01:19:46.323 --> 01:19:47.157
Oh.

01:20:28.323 --> 01:20:29.908
THANKS TO CHO JUNG-SEOK AND JEON MI-DO,
OUR FOREVER LEE IK-JUN AND CHAE SONG-HWA,

01:20:29.991 --> 01:20:31.701
FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCES

01:20:32.619 --> 01:20:34.704
RESIDENT PLAYBOOK

01:20:36.581 --> 01:20:37.332
The two of them?

01:20:37.833 --> 01:20:38.375
Where?

01:20:38.875 --> 01:20:39.918
What the heck?

01:20:40.418 --> 01:20:42.254
-You're so cute.
-Oh? Is it Doctor Ku?

01:20:42.337 --> 01:20:44.047
Hey, this is insane, come on, come on!

01:20:44.130 --> 01:20:45.215
-Just trust me!
-Doctor,

01:20:45.298 --> 01:20:46.258
there's no need to worry.

01:20:46.758 --> 01:20:48.760
I pride myself on loyalty
above everything else in life.

01:20:48.844 --> 01:20:49.886
Pleased to meet you.

01:20:49.970 --> 01:20:51.513
I'm Yi-young's friend, Pyo Nam-kyung.

01:20:51.596 --> 01:20:53.181
-Yi-young's been-
-Stop it.

01:20:53.265 --> 01:20:56.309
-All right, here we go again.
-Seong-chan.

01:20:56.393 --> 01:20:58.186
You broke down in tears
yesterday saying he's

01:20:58.270 --> 01:20:59.980
your father, and today, he's your son?

01:21:00.063 --> 01:21:01.314
What do you think you're doing?

01:21:01.398 --> 01:21:03.525
-You shouldn't be touching this Sir.
-Oh Yi-young!

01:21:03.608 --> 01:21:05.735
I would like…
for you to only focus on your labor today

01:21:05.819 --> 01:21:07.153
-What?
-No,

01:21:07.237 --> 01:21:08.363
she can't go.

01:21:08.446 --> 01:21:09.364
It's just out! The
umbilical cord just fell out!

01:21:09.447 --> 01:21:11.157
Hey, why don't you come
up here yourself right now?

01:21:11.241 --> 01:21:12.284
What're you staring at?

01:21:12.367 --> 01:21:13.368
Professor.

01:21:13.451 --> 01:21:15.620
I do hope you recall the request
that I made earlier?

01:21:15.704 --> 01:21:17.497
If it's what the patient wants,
I have no choice.

01:21:17.581 --> 01:21:19.457
Oh Yi-young,
move to the lead surgeon's spot.

01:21:19.541 --> 01:21:20.083
Wait, what?

01:21:20.584 --> 01:21:22.252
Will our Obstetrics department's legend

01:21:22.335 --> 01:21:23.795
work on Oh Yi-young, too?

01:21:23.879 --> 01:21:26.131
-Where's Um Jae-il?
-Why would you two go there at

01:21:26.214 --> 01:21:28.800
night? It's not like you're lovers.
Did Um Jae-il tell you that he likes you?

01:21:28.884 --> 01:21:30.135
Hey, are you guys dating?

01:21:30.218 --> 01:21:32.345
Does, he actually want us to date?
